#. column 31: The people of the Twelveswood are always looking for those willing to assist them. Unfortunately, you still look a tad green to be of any real help. Now if <switch $n1><case>someone such as Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>someone such as Momodi Modi</switch> were to vouch for you, that would be a different story...
#. column 32: The quest you were assigned is of the utmost import. May the Matron see you to success.
#. column 34: Well done, adventurer. The levewatch overseeing your duty was thoroughly impressed. You may take your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Oh, and I have seen to it that the bounty of the wanted target you most bravely slew was included.
#. macro: <switch $n1><case>someone such as Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>someone such as Momodi Modi</switch> — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:5:0:33"
msgid "The people of the Twelveswood are always looking for those willing to assist them. Unfortunately, you still look a tad green to be of any real help. Now if <switch $n1><case>someone such as Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>someone such as Momodi Modi</switch> were to vouch for you, that would be a different story..."
msgstr "Жители Леса Двенадцати всегда рады тем, кто готов им помочь. Жаль только, что вы пока зелёный новичок и толку от вас будет немного. Вот если бы за вас поручился кто-нибудь вроде <switch $n1><case>Бадерона Десятипалого<case>Матери Миунне<case>Момоди Моди</switch>, тогда другое дело..."

#. ja: ギルドリーヴ報酬の受け取りですね？<br>この任務を成し遂げるとは……お見事です。<br>どうぞ、こちらが規定の報酬ですよ。
#. de: Gut gemacht, <if $gn4>Abenteurerin<else>Abenteurer</if>. Unsere Beobachter waren von deinen Fertigkeiten beeindruckt. Hier ist deine Belohnung.
#. fr: Ah, vous avez rempli votre mission<nbsp>! Parfait, beau travail. Voici la récompense, comme promis.
#. column 30: The people of the Twelveswood need your help, adventurer. Have you the courage to provide it?
#. column 31: The people of the Twelveswood are always looking for those willing to assist them. Unfortunately, you still look a tad green to be of any real help. Now if <switch $n1><case>someone such as Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>someone such as Momodi Modi</switch> were to vouch for you, that would be a different story...
#. column 32: The quest you were assigned is of the utmost import. May the Matron see you to success.
#. column 33: The people of the Twelveswood are always looking for those willing to assist them. Unfortunately, you still look a tad green to be of any real help. Now if <switch $n1><case>someone such as Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>someone such as Momodi Modi</switch> were to vouch for you, that would be a different story...
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Oh, and I have seen to it that the bounty of the wanted target you most bravely slew was included.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:5:0:34"
msgid "Well done, adventurer. The levewatch overseeing your duty was thoroughly impressed. You may take your reward."
msgstr "Отличная работа, искатель приключений! Наблюдатель, следивший за вашим заданием, остался под большим впечатлением. Вот ваша награда."

#. ja: すばらしいですね。<br>手配されていた賞金首まで倒してしまうだなんて。<br>もちろん報酬にも色を付けておきますよ。
#. de: Ich habe auch dafür gesorgt, dass das Kopfgeld für das gesuchte Ziel darin enthalten ist.
#. fr: Vous êtes venu<if $gn4>e</if> à bout d'un monstre dont la tête était mise à prix<nbsp>!? Merci infiniment<nbsp>! Grâce à vous, la forêt de Sombrelinceul sera un peu moins dangereuse. Tenez, votre récompense...
#. column 30: The people of the Twelveswood need your help, adventurer. Have you the courage to provide it?
#. column 31: The people of the Twelveswood are always looking for those willing to assist them. Unfortunately, you still look a tad green to be of any real help. Now if <switch $n1><case>someone such as Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>someone such as Momodi Modi</switch> were to vouch for you, that would be a different story...
#. column 32: The quest you were assigned is of the utmost import. May the Matron see you to success.
#. column 33: The people of the Twelveswood are always looking for those willing to assist them. Unfortunately, you still look a tad green to be of any real help. Now if <switch $n1><case>someone such as Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>someone such as Momodi Modi</switch> were to vouch for you, that would be a different story...
#. column 34: Well done, adventurer. The levewatch overseeing your duty was thoroughly impressed. You may take your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:5:0:37"
msgid "Oh, and I have seen to it that the bounty of the wanted target you most bravely slew was included."
msgstr "К тому же я позаботился о том, чтобы включить в награду плату за голову разыскиваемой твари, которую вы так храбро одолели."

#. ja: リムサ・ロミンサ都市民をはじめ、<br>近隣の住民なんかから届いた依頼を<br>ギルドリーヴとして発行しているよ。
#. de: Herbei, herbei! Erstklassige Freibriefe für jeden Geschmack!
#. fr: Salut<nbsp>! Si tu cherches des mandats, tu es au bon endrrroit.
#. column 31: Welcome! The people of Eorzea are in constant need of a helping hand. Might you know of anyone talented in the arts of battle or spellcraft? You? Oh no, <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> would have my head on a platter if I were to allow one as green as you take on the tasks I've been entrusted.
#. column 32: Godsspeed to you then!
#. column 33: Welcome! The people of Eorzea are in constant need of a helping hand. Might you know of anyone talented in the arts of battle or spellcraft? You? Oh no, the guildmaster would have my head on a platter if I were to allow one as green as you take on the tasks I've been entrusted.
#. column 34: Excellent. The levewatches have reported, and I have used their evaluation to tally your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: The extra gil you see included is the bounty for the wanted target you slew.
#. macro: <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:6:0:30"
msgid "Welcome, welcome! The people of Eorzea are in desperate need of a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your talents. Might I interest you in a leve or two?"
msgstr "Добро пожаловать! В Эорзее позарез нужен <if $gn4>талантливый человек<else>талантливый человек</if>. Не желаете взять одно-два поручения?"

#. ja: 仕事を探しているんなら、良いところに来たね。<br>ここでは、実力ある冒険者に「ギルドリーヴ」の<br>仕事を発行しているのさ。<br>ただし、まずは冒険者ギルドの世話役、<br><switch $n1><case>バデロン<case>ミューヌ<case>モモディ</switch>さんからの紹介を受けるんだね。<br>そうすれば、いつでも仕事を回させてもらうよ。
#. de: Du? Ah, das tut mir leid, <if $gn4>mein Kind<else>mein Freund</if>, aber so hoffnungsvoll du auch aussiehst, für einen Neuling wie dich hab ich noch nichts. Oder willst du, dass <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> mich kaltstellt?
#. fr: Ce que je fais ici<nbsp>? Eh bien, je propose des mandats aux aven<shy>tu<shy>rrriers rattachés à la guilde. Le travail ne manque pas en ce moment, d'ailleurs ton aide serait la bienvenue. Hélas, tu manques encore un peu d'expérience pour cela... Reviens me voir quand <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> t'aurrra donné son aval et je m'occuperai de toi.
#. column 30: Welcome, welcome! The people of Eorzea are in desperate need of a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your talents. Might I interest you in a leve or two?
#. column 32: Godsspeed to you then!
#. column 33: Welcome! The people of Eorzea are in constant need of a helping hand. Might you know of anyone talented in the arts of battle or spellcraft? You? Oh no, the guildmaster would have my head on a platter if I were to allow one as green as you take on the tasks I've been entrusted.
#. column 34: Excellent. The levewatches have reported, and I have used their evaluation to tally your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: The extra gil you see included is the bounty for the wanted target you slew.
#. macro: <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:6:0:31"
msgid "Welcome! The people of Eorzea are in constant need of a helping hand. Might you know of anyone talented in the arts of battle or spellcraft? You? Oh no, <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> would have my head on a platter if I were to allow one as green as you take on the tasks I've been entrusted."
msgstr "Добро пожаловать! Жителям Эорзеи всегда нужна помощь. Не знаете кого-нибудь, кто умеет сражаться или колдовать? Вас? О нет, <switch $n1><case>Бадерон Десятипалый<case>Мать Миунне<case>Момоди Моди</switch> мне головы не сносит, если я доверю порученное мне дело такому зелёному новичку, как вы."

#. ja: それじゃ、気をつけていってらっしゃい！
#. de: Na, dann viel Erfolg!
#. fr: Bonne chance, et sois prrrudent<if $gn4>e</if><nbsp>!
#. column 30: Welcome, welcome! The people of Eorzea are in desperate need of a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your talents. Might I interest you in a leve or two?
#. column 31: Welcome! The people of Eorzea are in constant need of a helping hand. Might you know of anyone talented in the arts of battle or spellcraft? You? Oh no, <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> would have my head on a platter if I were to allow one as green as you take on the tasks I've been entrusted.
#. column 33: Welcome! The people of Eorzea are in constant need of a helping hand. Might you know of anyone talented in the arts of battle or spellcraft? You? Oh no, the guildmaster would have my head on a platter if I were to allow one as green as you take on the tasks I've been entrusted.
#. column 34: Excellent. The levewatches have reported, and I have used their evaluation to tally your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: The extra gil you see included is the bounty for the wanted target you slew.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:6:0:32"
msgid "Godsspeed to you then!"
msgstr "Ну, счастливого пути!"

#. ja: 仕事を探しているんなら、良いところに来たね。<br>ここでは、実力ある冒険者に「ギルドリーヴ」の<br>仕事を発行しているのさ。<br>ただし、まずはこの辺りの魔物を、<br>ちょちょいと片付けられる実力を付けるんだね。<br>そうすれば、いつでも仕事を回させてもらうよ。
#. de: Willkommen! Bei uns gibt es immer Arbeit für diejenigen, die keine Gefahren scheuen. Du kennst nicht zufällig jemanden, der geübt im Kampf oder in der Zauberkunst wäre? Geübter als du, meine ich. Einem Neuling wie dir kann ich keinesfalls einen Auftrag überlassen.
#. fr: Ce que je fais ici<nbsp>? Eh bien, je propose des mandats aux aven<shy>tu<shy>rrriers rattachés à la guilde. Le travail ne manque pas en ce moment, d'ailleurs ton aide serait la bienvenue. Hélas, tu manques encore un peu d'expérience pour cela... Il faut que tu progresses encore et que tu deviennes suf<shy>fi<shy>sam<shy>ment fort<if $gn4>e</if> pour abattre les monstres qui rôdent autourrr de Limsa Lominsa<nbsp>; sinon je ne donne pas cher de ta peau.
#. column 30: Welcome, welcome! The people of Eorzea are in desperate need of a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your talents. Might I interest you in a leve or two?
#. column 31: Welcome! The people of Eorzea are in constant need of a helping hand. Might you know of anyone talented in the arts of battle or spellcraft? You? Oh no, <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> would have my head on a platter if I were to allow one as green as you take on the tasks I've been entrusted.
#. column 32: Godsspeed to you then!
#. column 34: Excellent. The levewatches have reported, and I have used their evaluation to tally your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: The extra gil you see included is the bounty for the wanted target you slew.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:6:0:33"
msgid "Welcome! The people of Eorzea are in constant need of a helping hand. Might you know of anyone talented in the arts of battle or spellcraft? You? Oh no, the guildmaster would have my head on a platter if I were to allow one as green as you take on the tasks I've been entrusted."
msgstr "Добро пожаловать! Жителям Эорзеи всегда нужна помощь. Не знаете кого-нибудь, кто умеет сражаться или колдовать? Вас? О нет, начальник гильдии мне головы не сносит, если я доверю порученное мне дело такому зелёному новичку, как вы."

#. ja: ギルドリーヴの達成報告だね？<br>お疲れさま、報酬を受け取ってね。<br>きっと依頼主も満足してると思うよ～。
#. de: Ausgezeichnet. Ich habe den Bericht der Beobachter empfangen und deine Belohnung bereitgelegt. Bitte sehr.
#. fr: Tu as fini<nbsp>? Bien, bien, bien... Voilà ta récompense. Le client sera rrravi, j'en suis sûre<nbsp>!
#. column 30: Welcome, welcome! The people of Eorzea are in desperate need of a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your talents. Might I interest you in a leve or two?
#. column 31: Welcome! The people of Eorzea are in constant need of a helping hand. Might you know of anyone talented in the arts of battle or spellcraft? You? Oh no, <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> would have my head on a platter if I were to allow one as green as you take on the tasks I've been entrusted.
#. column 32: Godsspeed to you then!
#. column 33: Welcome! The people of Eorzea are in constant need of a helping hand. Might you know of anyone talented in the arts of battle or spellcraft? You? Oh no, the guildmaster would have my head on a platter if I were to allow one as green as you take on the tasks I've been entrusted.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: The extra gil you see included is the bounty for the wanted target you slew.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:6:0:34"
msgid "Excellent. The levewatches have reported, and I have used their evaluation to tally your reward."
msgstr "Отлично. Наблюдатели прислали отчёт, и я уже подсчитал вашу награду."

#. ja: ギルドリーヴの達成報告だね……<br>って、手配中の賞金首まで仕留めたの？<br>すごいね、報酬も上乗せしちゃうよ。
#. de: Die Belohnung kann sich sehen lassen, was? Darin ist ja auch das Kopfgeld für das gesuchte Ziel enthalten, das du erschlagen hast.
#. fr: Ça y est, tu as rempli ta mission<nbsp>? Quoi<nbsp>? Tu as abattu un monstre dont la tête était mise à prix<nbsp>!? Mais c'est forrrmidable<nbsp>! Tu mérites une récompense sup<shy>plé<shy>men<shy>tai<shy>re.
#. column 30: Welcome, welcome! The people of Eorzea are in desperate need of a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your talents. Might I interest you in a leve or two?
#. column 31: Welcome! The people of Eorzea are in constant need of a helping hand. Might you know of anyone talented in the arts of battle or spellcraft? You? Oh no, <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> would have my head on a platter if I were to allow one as green as you take on the tasks I've been entrusted.
#. column 32: Godsspeed to you then!
#. column 33: Welcome! The people of Eorzea are in constant need of a helping hand. Might you know of anyone talented in the arts of battle or spellcraft? You? Oh no, the guildmaster would have my head on a platter if I were to allow one as green as you take on the tasks I've been entrusted.
#. column 34: Excellent. The levewatches have reported, and I have used their evaluation to tally your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:6:0:37"
msgid "The extra gil you see included is the bounty for the wanted target you slew."
msgstr "В придачу к награде я добавил деньги за голову разыскиваемой твари, которую вы убили."

#. ja: ウルダハ都市民をはじめ、<br>さまざまな人々から寄せられた依頼を<br>ギルドリーヴとして発行しています。
#. de: Seid gegrüßt, <if $gn4>Abenteurerin<else>Abenteurer</if>. Ich bin für das Ausstellen von Freibriefen zuständig.
#. fr: <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>Bonsoir<else>Bonjour</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>Bonjour<else>Bonsoir</if></if>, mon ami<if $gn4>e</if>. Je propose des mandats aux aventuriers en fonction des demandes qui nous parviennent à la guilde.
#. column 31: My apologies, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>, but I am not authorized to issue guildleves to those as new to adventuring as you appear to be. Perhaps you should <switch $n1><case>return to Limsa Lominsa and speak with Baderon Tenfingers of the Drowning Wench<case>return to Gridania and speak with Mother Miounne of the Carline Canopy<case>speak with Momodi Modi across the hall</switch> and see if <switch $n1><case>he<case>she<case>she</switch> cannot point you in the right direction.
#. column 32: May the Traders see you to fortune.
#. column 33: My apologies, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>, but I am not authorized to issue guildleves to those as new to adventuring as you appear to be. It might serve you well to step outside the city walls and see the world before running headlong into tasks that will only put your precious life in danger.
#. column 34: I take it the quest was a success. Or, at least that is what the levewatches tell me. I have your reward right here.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Ah, and the extra coin─that is the bounty you earned by slaying the wanted target. The Brass Blades extend their gratitude for your service to the sultanate.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:7:0:30"
msgid "Greetings, adventurer. I deal in the issuing of guildleves."
msgstr "Приветствую, искатель приключений. Я выдаю гильдейские поручения."

#. ja: ひょっとして、お仕事をお探しですか？<br>ここでは、ある程度の経験を持つ冒険者の方に、<br>「ギルドリーヴ」の仕事を発行しております。<br>冒険者ギルドの世話役である<br><switch $n1><case>バデロン氏<case>ミューヌ女史<case>モモディ女史</switch>からの紹介がありましたら、<br>是非とも、リーヴを依頼させていただきたく思います。
#. de: Verzeiht, <if $gn4>meine Dame<else>mein Herr</if>, aber ich bin nicht dazu autorisiert, Freibriefe an Neulinge wie Euch auszustellen. Vielleicht solltet Ihr <switch $n1><case>nach Limsa Lominsa zurückkehren und ein Wörtchen mit Baderon in der Hafenbar „Zur Ertränkten Sorge“ wechseln<case>nach Gridania zurückkehren und mit Miounne in ihrem Hexenstübchen sprechen<case>Euch an Momodi auf der anderen Seite der Halle wenden</switch>. Dort werdet Ihr geeignete Arbeit finden.
#. fr: Ce que je fais ici<nbsp>? Eh bien, je propose des mandats aux aventuriers rattachés à la guilde. Le travail ne manque pas en ce moment, d'ailleurs votre aide serait la bienvenue. Hélas, vous manquez encore un peu d'expérience pour cela... Revenez me voir quand vous aurez l'au<shy>to<shy>ri<shy>sa<shy>tion de <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> et je m'occuperai de vous.
#. column 30: Greetings, adventurer. I deal in the issuing of guildleves.
#. column 32: May the Traders see you to fortune.
#. column 33: My apologies, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>, but I am not authorized to issue guildleves to those as new to adventuring as you appear to be. It might serve you well to step outside the city walls and see the world before running headlong into tasks that will only put your precious life in danger.
#. column 34: I take it the quest was a success. Or, at least that is what the levewatches tell me. I have your reward right here.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Ah, and the extra coin─that is the bounty you earned by slaying the wanted target. The Brass Blades extend their gratitude for your service to the sultanate.
#. macro: <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <switch $n1><case>return to Limsa Lominsa and speak with Baderon Tenfingers of the Drowning Wench<case>return to Gridania and speak with Mother Miounne of the C… — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <switch $n1><case>he<case>she<case>she</switch> — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:7:0:31"
msgid "My apologies, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>, but I am not authorized to issue guildleves to those as new to adventuring as you appear to be. Perhaps you should <switch $n1><case>return to Limsa Lominsa and speak with Baderon Tenfingers of the Drowning Wench<case>return to Gridania and speak with Mother Miounne of the Carline Canopy<case>speak with Momodi Modi across the hall</switch> and see if <switch $n1><case>he<case>she<case>she</switch> cannot point you in the right direction."
msgstr "Прошу прощения, <if $gn4>сударыня<else>сударь</if>, но я не вправе выдавать поручения таким неопытным в приключениях, как вы. Попробуйте <switch $n1><case>вернуться в Лимсу Ломинсу и поговорить с Бадероном Десятипалым в таверне<case>вернуться в Гриданию и поговорить с Матерью Миунне<case>поговорить с Момоди Моди через зал</switch>. Возможно, <switch $n1><case>он<case>она<case>она</switch> подскажет, что делать дальше."

#. ja: さあ、頑張ってください。<br>吉報をお待ちしておりますよ。
#. de: Mögen die Kaufleute Euch Glück und Wohlstand bringen.
#. fr: Bonne chance, et que les Douze veillent sur vous...
#. column 30: Greetings, adventurer. I deal in the issuing of guildleves.
#. column 31: My apologies, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>, but I am not authorized to issue guildleves to those as new to adventuring as you appear to be. Perhaps you should <switch $n1><case>return to Limsa Lominsa and speak with Baderon Tenfingers of the Drowning Wench<case>return to Gridania and speak with Mother Miounne of the Carline Canopy<case>speak with Momodi Modi across the hall</switch> and see if <switch $n1><case>he<case>she<case>she</switch> cannot point you in the right direction.
#. column 33: My apologies, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>, but I am not authorized to issue guildleves to those as new to adventuring as you appear to be. It might serve you well to step outside the city walls and see the world before running headlong into tasks that will only put your precious life in danger.
#. column 34: I take it the quest was a success. Or, at least that is what the levewatches tell me. I have your reward right here.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Ah, and the extra coin─that is the bounty you earned by slaying the wanted target. The Brass Blades extend their gratitude for your service to the sultanate.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:7:0:32"
msgid "May the Traders see you to fortune."
msgstr "Пусть Торговцы пошлют вам удачу."

#. ja: ひょっとして、お仕事をお探しですか？<br>ここでは、ある程度の経験を持つ冒険者の方に、<br>「ギルドリーヴ」の仕事を発行しております。<br>あなたに、この近辺の魔物を<br>容易く倒せるほどの実力が身についたときには、<br>是非とも、リーヴを依頼させていただきたく思います。
#. de: Verzeiht, <if $gn4>meine Dame<else>mein Herr</if>, aber ich bin nicht dazu autorisiert, Freibriefe an Neulinge wie Euch auszustellen. Warum verlasst Ihr die Stadt nicht für eine Weile und schaut Euch die große, weite Welt an? Das Leben ist spannend dort draußen.
#. fr: Ce que je fais ici<nbsp>? Eh bien, je propose des mandats aux aventuriers rattachés à la guilde. Le travail ne manque pas en ce moment, d'ailleurs votre aide serait la bienvenue. Hélas, vous manquez encore un peu d'expérience pour cela... Il faut que vous progressiez encore et que vous deveniez suf<shy>fi<shy>sam<shy>ment fort<if $gn4>e</if> pour abattre les monstres qui rôdent autour d'Ul'dah.
#. column 30: Greetings, adventurer. I deal in the issuing of guildleves.
#. column 31: My apologies, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>, but I am not authorized to issue guildleves to those as new to adventuring as you appear to be. Perhaps you should <switch $n1><case>return to Limsa Lominsa and speak with Baderon Tenfingers of the Drowning Wench<case>return to Gridania and speak with Mother Miounne of the Carline Canopy<case>speak with Momodi Modi across the hall</switch> and see if <switch $n1><case>he<case>she<case>she</switch> cannot point you in the right direction.
#. column 32: May the Traders see you to fortune.
#. column 34: I take it the quest was a success. Or, at least that is what the levewatches tell me. I have your reward right here.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Ah, and the extra coin─that is the bounty you earned by slaying the wanted target. The Brass Blades extend their gratitude for your service to the sultanate.
#. macro: <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:7:0:33"
msgid "My apologies, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>, but I am not authorized to issue guildleves to those as new to adventuring as you appear to be. It might serve you well to step outside the city walls and see the world before running headlong into tasks that will only put your precious life in danger."
msgstr "Прошу прощения, <if $gn4>сударыня<else>сударь</if>, но я не вправе выдавать поручения таким неопытным в приключениях, как вы. Лучше выйдите за городские стены и посмотрите мир, прежде чем бросаться в опасные дела и рисковать жизнью."

#. ja: お帰りなさいませ。<br>どうやら、無事に任務を達成された様子……<br>ご苦労様でした。報酬をお受け取りください。
#. de: Habt Ihr den Auftrag erfolgreich ausgeführt? So berichten es jedenfalls die Beobachter. Hier, Eure Belohnung.
#. fr: Ah, vous revoilà. Tout s'est bien passé, on dirait. Tenez, c'est votre récompense. Au plaisir de vous revoir<nbsp>!
#. column 30: Greetings, adventurer. I deal in the issuing of guildleves.
#. column 31: My apologies, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>, but I am not authorized to issue guildleves to those as new to adventuring as you appear to be. Perhaps you should <switch $n1><case>return to Limsa Lominsa and speak with Baderon Tenfingers of the Drowning Wench<case>return to Gridania and speak with Mother Miounne of the Carline Canopy<case>speak with Momodi Modi across the hall</switch> and see if <switch $n1><case>he<case>she<case>she</switch> cannot point you in the right direction.
#. column 32: May the Traders see you to fortune.
#. column 33: My apologies, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>, but I am not authorized to issue guildleves to those as new to adventuring as you appear to be. It might serve you well to step outside the city walls and see the world before running headlong into tasks that will only put your precious life in danger.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Ah, and the extra coin─that is the bounty you earned by slaying the wanted target. The Brass Blades extend their gratitude for your service to the sultanate.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:7:0:34"
msgid "I take it the quest was a success. Or, at least that is what the levewatches tell me. I have your reward right here."
msgstr "Полагаю, вы успешно выполнили поручение. По крайней мере, так говорят наблюдатели. Вот ваша награда."

#. ja: 賞金首まで倒してしまうだなんて、驚きましたよ。<br>さぞかし苦労なされたことでしょう。<br>是非とも、この報酬をお受け取りください。
#. de: Ihr meint den Zuschlag? Der ist dafür, dass Ihr das gesuchte Ziel zur Strecke gebracht habt.
#. fr: Vous avez tué un monstre dont la tête était mise à prix<nbsp>!? Mes félicitations<nbsp>! J'imagine que ça n'a pas dû être chose aisée... Vous méritez bien une petite récompense sup<shy>plé<shy>men<shy>tai<shy>re<nbsp>!
#. column 30: Greetings, adventurer. I deal in the issuing of guildleves.
#. column 31: My apologies, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>, but I am not authorized to issue guildleves to those as new to adventuring as you appear to be. Perhaps you should <switch $n1><case>return to Limsa Lominsa and speak with Baderon Tenfingers of the Drowning Wench<case>return to Gridania and speak with Mother Miounne of the Carline Canopy<case>speak with Momodi Modi across the hall</switch> and see if <switch $n1><case>he<case>she<case>she</switch> cannot point you in the right direction.
#. column 32: May the Traders see you to fortune.
#. column 33: My apologies, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>, but I am not authorized to issue guildleves to those as new to adventuring as you appear to be. It might serve you well to step outside the city walls and see the world before running headlong into tasks that will only put your precious life in danger.
#. column 34: I take it the quest was a success. Or, at least that is what the levewatches tell me. I have your reward right here.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:7:0:37"
msgid "Ah, and the extra coin─that is the bounty you earned by slaying the wanted target. The Brass Blades extend their gratitude for your service to the sultanate."
msgstr "А эти дополнительные монеты — награда за голову разыскиваемого преступника. Медные жала благодарят вас за службу султанату."

#. ja: こんにちは。<br>私は、この辺りの住人から寄せられた依頼を、<br>ギルドリーヴとして発行しています。
#. de: Den Zwölf zum Gruße! Für <if $gn4>eine ehrgeizige Abenteurerin<else>einen ehrgeizigen Abenteurer</if> gibt es hier immer etwas zu tun.
#. fr: <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>Bonsoir<else>Bonjour</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>Bonjour<else>Bonsoir</if></if> aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if><nbsp>! Je suis Totonowa, le responsable des mandats de guilde à Horizon.
#. column 31: You appear eager to serve the realm. This is good! Unfortunately, you do not appear to be of body <i>or</i> mind to serve her that well. This is bad. Speak with <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> to see if there is any way we might loosen this knotty situation we find ourselves in.
#. column 32: For coin and country!
#. column 33: You appear eager to serve the realm. This is good! Unfortunately, you do not appear to be of body <i>or</i> mind to serve her that well. This is bad. Whet your blade...or bow, or staff, or whatever may be your weapon of choice on some of the poor creatures crawling about the area and speak to me again when you are ready to take on the world...or at least the world immediately outside the city walls.
#. column 34: The levewatches were impressed, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>! Here is your well-earned reward!
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Oh, and don't let me forget this bounty. That was a noble display out there!
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:8:0:30"
msgid "The realm is always in need of eager volunteers to tend to those tedious tasks which need tending. You have a certain air of eagerness about you. Try your hand at a levequest?"
msgstr "Королевству всегда нужны добровольцы, готовые браться за всякую скучную работу. А у вас, похоже, есть к этому охота. Не хотите попробовать выполнить поручение?"

#. ja: こんにちは。<br>私は、この辺りの住人から寄せられた依頼を、<br>ギルドリーヴとして発行しています。<br>ですが、<switch $n1><case>チャ・モクリさん<case>ゴントランさん<case>ユースタスさん</switch>から、<br>仕事を任されるくらいの力量が必要となります。<br>そうでなければ、リーヴはお任せできませんよ。
#. de: Diesen Tatendrang lob ich mir! Leider mangelt es noch an etwas an Erfahrung und Können. <switch $n1><case>Sprich mit Baderon und lass dich auf ein paar Abenteuer schicken<case>Sprecht mit Miounne und lasst Euch auf ein paar Abenteuer schicken<case>Sprich mit Momodi und lass dich auf ein paar Abenteuer schicken</switch>, um den Umgang mit dem Schwert, Zauberstab oder einer anderen Waffe der Wahl zu üben.
#. fr: Vous cherchez du travail<nbsp>? Ça tombe bien, j'ai plusieurs mandats en réserve pour les aventuriers un peu rôdés. Autrement dit, je n'ai rien pour vous pour l'instant. Ha ha ha<nbsp>! Repassez me voir quand vous aurez la re<shy>com<shy>man<shy>da<shy>tion <switch $n1><case>de T'mokkri<case>de Gontrant<case>d'Eustace</switch> et je trouverai de quoi vous occuper.
#. column 30: The realm is always in need of eager volunteers to tend to those tedious tasks which need tending. You have a certain air of eagerness about you. Try your hand at a levequest?
#. column 32: For coin and country!
#. column 33: You appear eager to serve the realm. This is good! Unfortunately, you do not appear to be of body <i>or</i> mind to serve her that well. This is bad. Whet your blade...or bow, or staff, or whatever may be your weapon of choice on some of the poor creatures crawling about the area and speak to me again when you are ready to take on the world...or at least the world immediately outside the city walls.
#. column 34: The levewatches were impressed, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>! Here is your well-earned reward!
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Oh, and don't let me forget this bounty. That was a noble display out there!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:8:0:31"
msgid "You appear eager to serve the realm. This is good! Unfortunately, you do not appear to be of body <i>or</i> mind to serve her that well. This is bad. Speak with <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> to see if there is any way we might loosen this knotty situation we find ourselves in."
msgstr "Вы рветесь послужить королевству. Это хорошо! Вот только ни телом, <i>ни</i> духом вы пока не готовы ему служить. А это уже плохо. Поговорите с <switch $n1><case>Бадероном<case>Матерью Миунне<case>Момоди</switch> и узнайте, нельзя ли как-нибудь распутать этот узел."

#. ja: それでは、ひと働き頼みますよ。
#. de: Für Ruhm und Reichtum!
#. fr: Bonne chance pour votre mandat<nbsp>! Je suis derrière vous.
#. column 30: The realm is always in need of eager volunteers to tend to those tedious tasks which need tending. You have a certain air of eagerness about you. Try your hand at a levequest?
#. column 31: You appear eager to serve the realm. This is good! Unfortunately, you do not appear to be of body <i>or</i> mind to serve her that well. This is bad. Speak with <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> to see if there is any way we might loosen this knotty situation we find ourselves in.
#. column 33: You appear eager to serve the realm. This is good! Unfortunately, you do not appear to be of body <i>or</i> mind to serve her that well. This is bad. Whet your blade...or bow, or staff, or whatever may be your weapon of choice on some of the poor creatures crawling about the area and speak to me again when you are ready to take on the world...or at least the world immediately outside the city walls.
#. column 34: The levewatches were impressed, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>! Here is your well-earned reward!
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Oh, and don't let me forget this bounty. That was a noble display out there!
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:8:0:32"
msgid "For coin and country!"
msgstr "За монету и родину!"

#. ja: こんにちは。<br>私は、この辺りの住人から寄せられた依頼を、<br>ギルドリーヴとして発行しています。<br>ですが、この辺りの魔物を、<br>やすやすと倒せるくらいの力量が必要となります。<br>そうでなければ、リーヴはお任せできませんよ。
#. de: Ah, übersprudelnder Tatendrang, den lob ich mir. Leider mangelt es noch etwas an Erfahrung und Können. In der Umgebung lauern viele Monster und Halunken, mit denen man sich messen könnte, um sich im Umgang mit dem Schwert, Zauberstab oder einer anderen Waffe der Wahl zu üben.
#. fr: Vous cherchez du travail<nbsp>? Ça tombe bien, j'ai plusieurs mandats en réserve pour les aventuriers un peu rôdés. Autrement dit, je n'ai rien pour vous pour l'instant. Ha ha ha<nbsp>!
#. column 30: The realm is always in need of eager volunteers to tend to those tedious tasks which need tending. You have a certain air of eagerness about you. Try your hand at a levequest?
#. column 31: You appear eager to serve the realm. This is good! Unfortunately, you do not appear to be of body <i>or</i> mind to serve her that well. This is bad. Speak with <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> to see if there is any way we might loosen this knotty situation we find ourselves in.
#. column 32: For coin and country!
#. column 34: The levewatches were impressed, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>! Here is your well-earned reward!
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Oh, and don't let me forget this bounty. That was a noble display out there!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:8:0:33"
msgid "You appear eager to serve the realm. This is good! Unfortunately, you do not appear to be of body <i>or</i> mind to serve her that well. This is bad. Whet your blade...or bow, or staff, or whatever may be your weapon of choice on some of the poor creatures crawling about the area and speak to me again when you are ready to take on the world...or at least the world immediately outside the city walls."
msgstr "Вы рветесь послужить королевству. Это хорошо! Вот только ни телом, <i>ни</i> духом вы пока не готовы ему служить. А это уже плохо. Потренируйтесь на местных тварях: наточите клинок... или лук, посох — что у вас там. Возвращайтесь, когда будете готовы покорить мир... или хотя бы окрестности города."

#. ja: 任務は達成できたようですね。<br>これで依頼人も満足なさることでしょう。<br>さて、お待ちかねの報酬を受け取ってくださいね。
#. de: Eine beachtliche Leistung! Hier ist die wohlverdiente Belohnung.
#. fr: Vous avez terminé le travail sans encombres, à ce que je vois. J'ai bien fait de vous confier cette mission. Tenez, voilà votre récompense.
#. column 30: The realm is always in need of eager volunteers to tend to those tedious tasks which need tending. You have a certain air of eagerness about you. Try your hand at a levequest?
#. column 31: You appear eager to serve the realm. This is good! Unfortunately, you do not appear to be of body <i>or</i> mind to serve her that well. This is bad. Speak with <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> to see if there is any way we might loosen this knotty situation we find ourselves in.
#. column 32: For coin and country!
#. column 33: You appear eager to serve the realm. This is good! Unfortunately, you do not appear to be of body <i>or</i> mind to serve her that well. This is bad. Whet your blade...or bow, or staff, or whatever may be your weapon of choice on some of the poor creatures crawling about the area and speak to me again when you are ready to take on the world...or at least the world immediately outside the city walls.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Oh, and don't let me forget this bounty. That was a noble display out there!
#. macro: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split> — the first name of the player character (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <string $gs1> — a text value passed to the string; value = global text 1 (the name of the player character) (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:8:0:34"
msgid "The levewatches were impressed, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>! Here is your well-earned reward!"
msgstr "Наблюдатели остались под впечатлением, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>! Вот ваша заслуженная награда!"

#. ja: 賞金首まで倒したですって？　流石ですね！<br>それでは報酬を上乗せさせてもらいましょう。<br>おめでとうございます。
#. de: Und auch das Kopfgeld darf ich nicht vergessen. Gute Leistung!
#. fr: Vous avez tué un monstre recherché, vous dites<nbsp>? Ouah... <if $gn4>Mademoiselle<else>Monsieur</if>, je vous tire mon chapeau<nbsp>! Tenez, voilà de quoi remplir votre bourse<nbsp>!
#. column 30: The realm is always in need of eager volunteers to tend to those tedious tasks which need tending. You have a certain air of eagerness about you. Try your hand at a levequest?
#. column 31: You appear eager to serve the realm. This is good! Unfortunately, you do not appear to be of body <i>or</i> mind to serve her that well. This is bad. Speak with <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> to see if there is any way we might loosen this knotty situation we find ourselves in.
#. column 32: For coin and country!
#. column 33: You appear eager to serve the realm. This is good! Unfortunately, you do not appear to be of body <i>or</i> mind to serve her that well. This is bad. Whet your blade...or bow, or staff, or whatever may be your weapon of choice on some of the poor creatures crawling about the area and speak to me again when you are ready to take on the world...or at least the world immediately outside the city walls.
#. column 34: The levewatches were impressed, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>! Here is your well-earned reward!
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:8:0:37"
msgid "Oh, and don't let me forget this bounty. That was a noble display out there!"
msgstr "И не забудьте про награду за голову. Вы там показали себя настоящим героем!"

#. ja: ドライボーン一帯に関する依頼を、<br>ギルドリーヴとして発行しています。
#. de: Guten <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>Abend<else>Morgen</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>Tag<else>Abend</if></if>, <if $gn4>Abenteurerin<else>Abenteurer</if>! Und ist es nicht ein schöner <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>Abend<else>Morgen</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>Tag<else>Abend</if></if> für einen Freibrief? Was sagst du?
#. fr: Bien le <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>bonsoir<else>bonjour</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>bonjour<else>bonsoir</if></if> aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>. J'ai en ma possession divers mandats de guilde, que je pourrai vous confier si vous êtes intéressé<if $gn4>e</if>.
#. column 31: Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> to you, adventurer. And a fine <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> it is, I say. A fine <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> to march back to the Adventurers' Guild in <switch $n1><case>Limsa<case>Gridania<case>Ul'dah</switch> and set yourself straight with <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>. Only then will I let you partake in some of these fine guildleves I hold here.
#. column 32: Off you are then! Time is of the essence!
#. column 33: Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> to you, adventurer. And a fine <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> it is, I say. A fine <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> to march back out into the field. Only then will I let you partake in some of these fine guildleves I hold here.
#. column 34: I see the desert heat wasn't too much for you. Here is your reward. See that you don't spend it all at the pub!
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Oh, and the bounty! It almost slipped my mind. I believe you'll be wanting this, as well. Unless, that is, you don't, because I would be more than happy to─ You <i>do</i> want it, then. Alright. I suppose that's only fair, considering <i>you</i> were the one who killed the fiend.
#. macro: <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 11 < 12 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 11 < 4 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 11 < 17 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:9:0:30"
msgid "Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> to you, adventurer. And a fine <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> it is, I say. A fine <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> for a levequest!"
msgstr "Добрый <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>вечер<else>день</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>день<else>вечер</if></if>, искатель приключений. И правда, славный <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>вечер<else>день</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>день<else>вечер</if></if>, скажу я вам. Самое время взяться за поручение!"

#. ja: 冒険者ギルドの同志ですね？<br>ここでは経験のある方に「ギルドリーヴ」の<br>仕事を発行させてもらっています。<br>ですが、まずはギルドの世話役、<br><switch $n1><case>バデロン<case>ミューヌ<case>モモディ</switch>さんからの紹介を受けてください。<br>そうすれば、仕事を斡旋させていただきますから。
#. de: Guten <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>Abend<else>Morgen</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>Tag<else>Abend</if></if>, <if $gn4>Abenteurerin<else>Abenteurer</if>! Und ist es nicht ein schöner <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>Abend<else>Morgen</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>Tag<else>Abend</if></if>, um zurück zur Aben<shy>teurer<shy>gilde von <switch $n1><case>Limsa<case>Gridania<case>Ul'dah</switch> zu marschieren und mit <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> zu sprechen? Denn vorher bekommst du keinen von meinen lukrativen Freibriefen angeboten.
#. fr: Il y a toujours du travail pour les aventuriers qualifiés au camp des Os desséchés. D'ailleurs votre aide serait la bienvenue. Hélas, vous manquez encore un peu d'expérience pour cela... Revenez me voir quand vous aurez l'au<shy>to<shy>ri<shy>sa<shy>tion de <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> et je m'occuperai de vous.
#. column 30: Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> to you, adventurer. And a fine <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> it is, I say. A fine <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> for a levequest!
#. column 32: Off you are then! Time is of the essence!
#. column 33: Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> to you, adventurer. And a fine <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> it is, I say. A fine <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> to march back out into the field. Only then will I let you partake in some of these fine guildleves I hold here.
#. column 34: I see the desert heat wasn't too much for you. Here is your reward. See that you don't spend it all at the pub!
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Oh, and the bounty! It almost slipped my mind. I believe you'll be wanting this, as well. Unless, that is, you don't, because I would be more than happy to─ You <i>do</i> want it, then. Alright. I suppose that's only fair, considering <i>you</i> were the one who killed the fiend.
