msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:10:0:33"
msgid "A lonely place, this Swiftperch. That don't mean there ain't work to be done...just not by the likes of an unbloodied fry like yerself. Till ye've shown ye can hold yer own, I'll entrust the safety of this godsforsaken corner of the realm to more capable hands."
msgstr "В Свифтперче одиноко. Но работа тут есть... только не для таких неоперившихся новичков, как вы. Пока не докажете, что способны постоять за себя, я доверю безопасность этого богами забытого уголка края более опытным людям."

#. ja: お戻りですか、ご苦労さまです。<br>依頼人も、さぞ喜んでいることでしょう。<br>さあ、報酬を受け取ってください。
#. de: Nicht schlecht, nicht schlecht. Das hast du gut hinbekommen. Hier sind deine Gil.
#. fr: On dirait que tu as réussi ce mandat sans encombre. Tiens, voici la récompense qui t'est due.
#. column 30: A lonely place, this Swiftperch. That don't mean there ain't work to be done.
#. column 31: A lonely place, this Swiftperch. That don't mean there ain't work to be done...just not by the likes of an unbloodied fry like yerself. Till <switch $n1><case>ol' Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>wee Momodi Modi</switch> hasn't signed off on ye, I'll entrust the safety of this godsforsaken corner of the realm to more capable hands.
#. column 32: I've me eye on ye and all, <if $gn4>lass<else>lad</if>. See the job's done right, like.
#. column 33: A lonely place, this Swiftperch. That don't mean there ain't work to be done...just not by the likes of an unbloodied fry like yerself. Till ye've shown ye can hold yer own, I'll entrust the safety of this godsforsaken corner of the realm to more capable hands.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Ah, but not afore ye take this bounty. I saw what ye did up there to the wanted cur, like. Not fleyed, were ye?
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:10:0:34"
msgid "A fair lick, that were. Let me ready yer coin now, so as ye can be on yer way."
msgstr "Неплохо справились. Сейчас выдам вам деньги, и можете отправляться дальше."

#. ja: なんですって、賞金首を討伐したのですか！<br>ふふふ、報酬をたっぷり差し上げなくてはなりませんね。
#. de: Und hier ist auch deine Belohnung. Dem gesuchten Ziel hast du es gezeigt und zwar nicht zu zimperlich.
#. fr: Non seulement tu as réussi ce mandat sans encombre, mais en plus tu as abattu une créature dont la tête était mise à prix<nbsp>!? C'est ce qui s'appelle faire d'une pierre deux coups<nbsp>! Bravo, tu as bien mérité ta récompense<nbsp>!
#. column 30: A lonely place, this Swiftperch. That don't mean there ain't work to be done.
#. column 31: A lonely place, this Swiftperch. That don't mean there ain't work to be done...just not by the likes of an unbloodied fry like yerself. Till <switch $n1><case>ol' Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>wee Momodi Modi</switch> hasn't signed off on ye, I'll entrust the safety of this godsforsaken corner of the realm to more capable hands.
#. column 32: I've me eye on ye and all, <if $gn4>lass<else>lad</if>. See the job's done right, like.
#. column 33: A lonely place, this Swiftperch. That don't mean there ain't work to be done...just not by the likes of an unbloodied fry like yerself. Till ye've shown ye can hold yer own, I'll entrust the safety of this godsforsaken corner of the realm to more capable hands.
#. column 34: A fair lick, that were. Let me ready yer coin now, so as ye can be on yer way.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:10:0:37"
msgid "Ah, but not afore ye take this bounty. I saw what ye did up there to the wanted cur, like. Not fleyed, were ye?"
msgstr "А вот и награда за голову. Видел я, как ты там расправился с разыскиваемой тварью. Не оробел, значит?"

#. ja: エールポートの住人をはじめ、<br>近隣地域から寄せられる依頼を、<br>ギルドリーヴとして発行しています。
#. de: Ich nehme an, du bist für die Freibriefe hier? Schau dich um, aber mach schnell, ich hab nicht den ganzen Tag Zeit.
#. fr: Salut <if $gn4>ma<else>mon</if> gaillard<if $gn4>e</if>. Si tu es venu<if $gn4>e</if> pour accomplir des mandats de guilde, tu t'es adressé<if $gn4>e</if> à la bonne personne.
#. column 31: Let me ask you someaught. Do you like this hat? I like this hat. It took me ten summers of lickin' ol' Baderon's boot to get this hat─a <i>levemete's</i> hat. I'd like to keep this hat, and doin' so means I's got to follow the rules. And rule number one? No leves to those what ain't proved them sen. Now back to the Adventurers' Guild with you.
#. column 32: Best of luck to you, then. If I'm not here when you get back, might be I'm in the pub.
#. column 33: Let me ask you someaught. Do you like this hat? I like this hat. It took me ten summers of lickin' ol' Baderon's boot to get this hat─a <i>levemete's</i> hat. I'd like to keep this hat, and doin' so means I's got to follow the rules. And rule number one? No leves to those what ain't proved them sen. Now back out into the bloody battlefields with you.
#. column 34: You'll not get a single gil from me while the leve's─ Hold on a tick... The levewatch tells me all is right as rain. I'll ready your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Then there's the wee matter of this bounty. I reckon you'll be lookin' to claim it.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:11:0:30"
msgid "I suppose you're here lookin' for some leves. Well, take your pick. But be quick about it. I haven't all day."
msgstr "Ищете поручения? Выбирайте, что душе угодно. Только побыстрее, у меня весь день не свободен."

#. ja: 実力ある冒険者の方に向けて、<br>「ギルドリーヴ」の仕事を発行しております。<br>ですが、この仕事を受けるには条件があるのです。<br>まずはギルドの顔役、<br><switch $n1><case>バデロン<case>ミューヌ<case>モモディ</switch>さんから紹介を受けてください。<br>それが最低限の条件なのですから。
#. de: Weißt du was? Ich hab 'nen ziemlich guten Job hier. Wenig Stress, gute Bezahlung, nette Leute ... na ja, meistens. Den Job würde ich gerne behalten. Und weißt du, was mich diesen wirklich guten Job kosten könnte? Wenn ich so einem Neuling wie dir einen Freibrief anvertraue. Also zurück zur Aben<shy>teurer<shy>gilde mit dir.
#. fr: Port-aux-Ales est un important lieu d'échanges commerciaux, ce n'est donc pas le travail qui manque ici. J'ai d'ailleurs plusieurs offres qui pourraient t'intéresser, malheureusement je ne suis pas autorisé à proposer des mandats aux aventuriers qui n'ont pas été recommandés par <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>.
#. column 30: I suppose you're here lookin' for some leves. Well, take your pick. But be quick about it. I haven't all day.
#. column 32: Best of luck to you, then. If I'm not here when you get back, might be I'm in the pub.
#. column 33: Let me ask you someaught. Do you like this hat? I like this hat. It took me ten summers of lickin' ol' Baderon's boot to get this hat─a <i>levemete's</i> hat. I'd like to keep this hat, and doin' so means I's got to follow the rules. And rule number one? No leves to those what ain't proved them sen. Now back out into the bloody battlefields with you.
#. column 34: You'll not get a single gil from me while the leve's─ Hold on a tick... The levewatch tells me all is right as rain. I'll ready your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Then there's the wee matter of this bounty. I reckon you'll be lookin' to claim it.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:11:0:31"
msgid "Let me ask you someaught. Do you like this hat? I like this hat. It took me ten summers of lickin' ol' Baderon's boot to get this hat─a <i>levemete's</i> hat. I'd like to keep this hat, and doin' so means I's got to follow the rules. And rule number one? No leves to those what ain't proved them sen. Now back to the Adventurers' Guild with you."
msgstr "Послушай-ка. Нравится тебе эта шляпа? Мне нравится. Десять лет я лизал сапоги старого Бадерона, чтобы её получить, — шляпу <i>распорядителя поручений</i>. Хочу её сохранить, а значит, придётся соблюдать правила. Правило номер один: поручений не давать тем, кто себя ещё не доказал. А теперь марш обратно в гильдию искателей приключений."

#. ja: 任務の成功を、心よりお祈りしていますよ。
#. de: Also los, worauf wartest du. Der Freibrief erledigt sich nicht vor alleine.
#. fr: Bon courage pour ton mandat. Moi, je vais en profiter pour me désaltérer avec quelques chopines pendant que tu te décarcasses. Hé hé hé<nbsp>!
#. column 30: I suppose you're here lookin' for some leves. Well, take your pick. But be quick about it. I haven't all day.
#. column 31: Let me ask you someaught. Do you like this hat? I like this hat. It took me ten summers of lickin' ol' Baderon's boot to get this hat─a <i>levemete's</i> hat. I'd like to keep this hat, and doin' so means I's got to follow the rules. And rule number one? No leves to those what ain't proved them sen. Now back to the Adventurers' Guild with you.
#. column 33: Let me ask you someaught. Do you like this hat? I like this hat. It took me ten summers of lickin' ol' Baderon's boot to get this hat─a <i>levemete's</i> hat. I'd like to keep this hat, and doin' so means I's got to follow the rules. And rule number one? No leves to those what ain't proved them sen. Now back out into the bloody battlefields with you.
#. column 34: You'll not get a single gil from me while the leve's─ Hold on a tick... The levewatch tells me all is right as rain. I'll ready your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Then there's the wee matter of this bounty. I reckon you'll be lookin' to claim it.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:11:0:32"
msgid "Best of luck to you, then. If I'm not here when you get back, might be I'm in the pub."
msgstr "Удачи. А если к твоему возвращению меня не будет, ищи в таверне."

#. ja: 実力ある冒険者の方に向けて、<br>「ギルドリーヴ」の仕事を発行しております。<br>ですが、この仕事を受けるには条件があるのです。<br>まずは、この近辺にいる恐ろしい魔物に<br>負けることのない実力を身につけてください。<br>それが最低限の条件なのですから。
#. de: Weißt du was? Ich hab 'nen ziemlich guten Job hier. Wenig Stress, gute Bezahlung, nette Leute ... na ja, meistens. Den Job würde ich gerne behalten. Und weißt du, was mich diesen wirklich guten Job kosten könnte? Wenn ich so einem Neuling wie dir einen Freibrief anvertraue. Also raus mit dir und komm nicht zurück, bevor du mehr Erfahrung da draußen gesammelt hast.
#. fr: Port-aux-Ales est un important lieu d'échanges commerciaux, ce n'est donc pas le travail qui manque ici. J'ai d'ailleurs plusieurs offres qui pourraient t'intéresser... malheureusement, je ne suis pas autorisé à proposer des mandats aux aventuriers débutants. Poursuis ton en<shy>traî<shy>ne<shy>ment et reviens me voir quand tu auras acquis un peu plus d'expérience.
#. column 30: I suppose you're here lookin' for some leves. Well, take your pick. But be quick about it. I haven't all day.
#. column 31: Let me ask you someaught. Do you like this hat? I like this hat. It took me ten summers of lickin' ol' Baderon's boot to get this hat─a <i>levemete's</i> hat. I'd like to keep this hat, and doin' so means I's got to follow the rules. And rule number one? No leves to those what ain't proved them sen. Now back to the Adventurers' Guild with you.
#. column 32: Best of luck to you, then. If I'm not here when you get back, might be I'm in the pub.
#. column 34: You'll not get a single gil from me while the leve's─ Hold on a tick... The levewatch tells me all is right as rain. I'll ready your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Then there's the wee matter of this bounty. I reckon you'll be lookin' to claim it.
