#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:11:0:33"
msgid "Let me ask you someaught. Do you like this hat? I like this hat. It took me ten summers of lickin' ol' Baderon's boot to get this hat─a <i>levemete's</i> hat. I'd like to keep this hat, and doin' so means I's got to follow the rules. And rule number one? No leves to those what ain't proved them sen. Now back out into the bloody battlefields with you."
msgstr "Послушай-ка. Нравится тебе эта шляпа? Мне нравится. Десять лет я лизал сапоги старого Бадерона, чтобы её получить, — шляпу <i>распорядителя поручений</i>. Хочу её сохранить, а значит, придётся соблюдать правила. Правило номер один: поручений не давать тем, кто себя ещё не доказал. А теперь марш обратно на поле боя."

#. ja: どうやら、無事に任務を果たせたようですね。<br>お疲れ様でした、報酬をお支払いしましょう。<br>依頼人もきっと満足していますよ。
#. de: Nicht einen Gil bekommst du, bevor du ... Moment, die Beobachter melden, dass der Auftrag erfüllt ist. Wurde ja auch Zeit. Hier ist deine Belohnung.
#. fr: On dirait que tu as réussi le mandat que je t'ai confié. Tiens, voilà ta récompense.
#. column 30: I suppose you're here lookin' for some leves. Well, take your pick. But be quick about it. I haven't all day.
#. column 31: Let me ask you someaught. Do you like this hat? I like this hat. It took me ten summers of lickin' ol' Baderon's boot to get this hat─a <i>levemete's</i> hat. I'd like to keep this hat, and doin' so means I's got to follow the rules. And rule number one? No leves to those what ain't proved them sen. Now back to the Adventurers' Guild with you.
#. column 32: Best of luck to you, then. If I'm not here when you get back, might be I'm in the pub.
#. column 33: Let me ask you someaught. Do you like this hat? I like this hat. It took me ten summers of lickin' ol' Baderon's boot to get this hat─a <i>levemete's</i> hat. I'd like to keep this hat, and doin' so means I's got to follow the rules. And rule number one? No leves to those what ain't proved them sen. Now back out into the bloody battlefields with you.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Then there's the wee matter of this bounty. I reckon you'll be lookin' to claim it.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:11:0:34"
msgid "You'll not get a single gil from me while the leve's─ Hold on a tick... The levewatch tells me all is right as rain. I'll ready your reward."
msgstr "Ни монеты не получишь, пока поручение не... Постой-ка. Наблюдатель доложил, что всё выполнено как надо. Сейчас приготовлю награду."

#. ja: どうやら、手配中の賞金首を討伐したようですね。<br>実に見事な働きぶり……報酬を増額せねばなりませんね。<br>本当に、お疲れ様でした。
#. de: Ach, und dann ist da ja noch das Kopfgeld. Bitte sehr.
#. fr: Alors comme ça, il paraît que tu as abattu une créature recherchée<nbsp>? C'est une excellente nouvelle<nbsp>! Tiens, j'ai ajouté un petit bonus à ta récompense, en guise de re<shy>mer<shy>cie<shy>ment.
#. column 30: I suppose you're here lookin' for some leves. Well, take your pick. But be quick about it. I haven't all day.
#. column 31: Let me ask you someaught. Do you like this hat? I like this hat. It took me ten summers of lickin' ol' Baderon's boot to get this hat─a <i>levemete's</i> hat. I'd like to keep this hat, and doin' so means I's got to follow the rules. And rule number one? No leves to those what ain't proved them sen. Now back to the Adventurers' Guild with you.
#. column 32: Best of luck to you, then. If I'm not here when you get back, might be I'm in the pub.
#. column 33: Let me ask you someaught. Do you like this hat? I like this hat. It took me ten summers of lickin' ol' Baderon's boot to get this hat─a <i>levemete's</i> hat. I'd like to keep this hat, and doin' so means I's got to follow the rules. And rule number one? No leves to those what ain't proved them sen. Now back out into the bloody battlefields with you.
#. column 34: You'll not get a single gil from me while the leve's─ Hold on a tick... The levewatch tells me all is right as rain. I'll ready your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:11:0:37"
msgid "Then there's the wee matter of this bounty. I reckon you'll be lookin' to claim it."
msgstr "И ещё тут награда за голову. Думаю, вы захотите её забрать."

#. ja: アンタも、いっちょまえの冒険者ヅラになってきたね。<br>ギルドリーヴで、ひと稼ぎするってのはどうだい？<br>アンタ向きの仕事が来てるんだ。
#. de: Du machst dich ja ganz ordentlich! Da könntest du dich glatt mal an ein paar Freibriefen versuchen, was meinst du?
#. fr: Eh, salut<nbsp>! T'as pas l'air com<shy>plè<shy>te<shy>ment bon<if $gn4>ne</if> à rien. Ça te dirait de gagner un peu d'argent avec un mandat<nbsp>? Je te trouverai quelque chose à ta portée.
#. column 31: I sense a certain weakness of both body and mind. I cannot assign a guildleve to one such as yourself. Perhaps good Mother Miounne has a task or two with which you might prove your skills.
#. column 32: The spirits are ever watching, my friend. Prove to them you are worthy of the duty you have been entrusted.
#. column 33: I sense a certain weakness of both body and mind. I cannot assign a guildleve to one such as yourself. Perhaps you might prove your skills on some lesser foes before attempting to take on those which lurk nearby.
#. column 34: You return in one piece, so I can only assume that the spirits approve of your deeds. Allow me to prepare your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And what is this? A little bird tells me that you have dispatched a wanted villain. That would make this bounty yours, as well.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:12:0:30"
msgid "You look to be of able mind and body. Might I interest you in a guildleve?"
msgstr "Выглядите вы человеком крепким и сообразительным. Не хотите взять гильдейское поручение?"

#. ja: アタシは冒険者ギルドの「ギルドリーヴ」担当官さ。<br>見たところ、アンタは冒険者としちゃ新米のようだね。<br><key>世話役の<switch $n1><case>バデロン<case>ミューヌ<case>モモディ</switch>に実力を認めさせ、<br>「ギルドリーヴ」の紹介を受けてから出直してきな。<br>そしたら、アンタにも仕事を斡旋してやるからさ。
#. de: Und wieder steht <if $gn4>eine Anfängerin<else>ein Anfänger</if> vor mir und will was erleben! Tja, wenn du einen Freibrief von mir willst, dann musst du erst mal <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> davon überzeugen, dass du genug auf dem Kasten hast. Frag <switch $n1><case>ihn<case>sie<case>sie</switch> doch mal nach einer passenden Aufgabe!
#. fr: Je fais partie de la guilde des aventuriers, figure-toi, et je propose des mandats aux aventuriers un peu rodés... mais pas aux bleus de ton genre. Reviens quand t'auras la re<shy>com<shy>man<shy>da<shy>tion de <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>, je te trouverai quelque chose... si t'es sage<nbsp>!
#. column 30: You look to be of able mind and body. Might I interest you in a guildleve?
#. column 32: The spirits are ever watching, my friend. Prove to them you are worthy of the duty you have been entrusted.
#. column 33: I sense a certain weakness of both body and mind. I cannot assign a guildleve to one such as yourself. Perhaps you might prove your skills on some lesser foes before attempting to take on those which lurk nearby.
#. column 34: You return in one piece, so I can only assume that the spirits approve of your deeds. Allow me to prepare your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And what is this? A little bird tells me that you have dispatched a wanted villain. That would make this bounty yours, as well.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:12:0:31"
msgid "I sense a certain weakness of both body and mind. I cannot assign a guildleve to one such as yourself. Perhaps good Mother Miounne has a task or two with which you might prove your skills."
msgstr "Чую я в вас слабость и телом, и духом. Не могу поручить вам такое дело. Может, добрая Матерь Миунне найдёт вам работу, на которой вы сможете показать себя."

#. ja: それじゃ、しっかり働いとくれ。<br>頼りにしてるんだから、しくじるんじゃないよ。
#. de: Also, auf geht's! Erledige das, was ich dir aufgetragen hab.
#. fr: Bon courage à toi. Me déçois pas, surtout<nbsp>!
#. column 30: You look to be of able mind and body. Might I interest you in a guildleve?
#. column 31: I sense a certain weakness of both body and mind. I cannot assign a guildleve to one such as yourself. Perhaps good Mother Miounne has a task or two with which you might prove your skills.
#. column 33: I sense a certain weakness of both body and mind. I cannot assign a guildleve to one such as yourself. Perhaps you might prove your skills on some lesser foes before attempting to take on those which lurk nearby.
#. column 34: You return in one piece, so I can only assume that the spirits approve of your deeds. Allow me to prepare your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And what is this? A little bird tells me that you have dispatched a wanted villain. That would make this bounty yours, as well.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:12:0:32"
msgid "The spirits are ever watching, my friend. Prove to them you are worthy of the duty you have been entrusted."
msgstr "Духи всегда наблюдают за вами, друг мой. Докажите им, что достойны порученного дела."

#. ja: アタシは冒険者ギルドの「ギルドリーヴ」担当官さ。<br>見たところ、アンタは冒険者としちゃ新米のようだね。<br><key>世話役の<switch $n1><case>バデロン<case>ミューヌ<case>モモディ</switch>に実力を認めさせ、<br>「ギルドリーヴ」の紹介を受けてから出直してきな。<br>そしたら、アンタにも仕事を斡旋してやるからさ。
#. de: Und wieder steht <if $gn4>eine Anfängerin<else>ein Anfänger</if> vor mir und will was erleben! Vielleicht solltest du dich erst mal an schwächeren Gegnern versuchen, bevor du es mit den Kreaturen in dieser Gegend aufnimmst.
#. fr: Je fais partie de la guilde des aventuriers, figure-toi, et je propose des mandats aux aventuriers un peu rodés... mais pas aux bleus de ton genre. Reviens quand t'auras la re<shy>com<shy>man<shy>da<shy>tion de <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>, je te trouverai quelque chose... si t'es sage<nbsp>!
#. column 30: You look to be of able mind and body. Might I interest you in a guildleve?
#. column 31: I sense a certain weakness of both body and mind. I cannot assign a guildleve to one such as yourself. Perhaps good Mother Miounne has a task or two with which you might prove your skills.
#. column 32: The spirits are ever watching, my friend. Prove to them you are worthy of the duty you have been entrusted.
#. column 34: You return in one piece, so I can only assume that the spirits approve of your deeds. Allow me to prepare your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And what is this? A little bird tells me that you have dispatched a wanted villain. That would make this bounty yours, as well.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:12:0:33"
msgid "I sense a certain weakness of both body and mind. I cannot assign a guildleve to one such as yourself. Perhaps you might prove your skills on some lesser foes before attempting to take on those which lurk nearby."
msgstr "Чую я в вас слабость и телом, и духом. Не могу поручить вам такое дело. Попробуйте сперва себя на мелких врагах, а уж потом беритесь за тех, кто водится поблизости."

#. ja: その面構えからすると、首尾は上々のようだね。<br>アンタもなかなかやるじゃないか。<br>ほら、報酬だよ、受け取りな！
#. de: Du bist in einem Stück zurückgekehrt. Die Gebieter scheinen mit deinen Taten zufrieden zu sein. Hier ist deine Belohnung.
#. fr: Je vois que t'as réussi ton coup. Bien joué... Tiens, voilà ta récompense<nbsp>!
#. column 30: You look to be of able mind and body. Might I interest you in a guildleve?
#. column 31: I sense a certain weakness of both body and mind. I cannot assign a guildleve to one such as yourself. Perhaps good Mother Miounne has a task or two with which you might prove your skills.
#. column 32: The spirits are ever watching, my friend. Prove to them you are worthy of the duty you have been entrusted.
#. column 33: I sense a certain weakness of both body and mind. I cannot assign a guildleve to one such as yourself. Perhaps you might prove your skills on some lesser foes before attempting to take on those which lurk nearby.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And what is this? A little bird tells me that you have dispatched a wanted villain. That would make this bounty yours, as well.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:12:0:34"
msgid "You return in one piece, so I can only assume that the spirits approve of your deeds. Allow me to prepare your reward."
msgstr "Вы вернулись целым и невредимым. Значит, духи одобряют ваши деяния. Позвольте приготовить вам награду."

#. ja: 賞金首を始末するだなんて、<br>アンタもなかなか、やるようだね。<br>さあ、報奨金を上乗せした報酬を受け取りな！
#. de: Sie flüstern mir auch, dass du das gesuchte Ziel erlegt hast. Dafür hast du dir einen besondere Belohnung verdient.
#. fr: Quoi<nbsp>? Non seulement t'as accompli le mandat, mais en plus t'as abattu un monstre recherché<nbsp>!? Alors là, je suis sur le cul<nbsp>! Oups<nbsp>! ça m'a échappé... Tiens, voilà ta récompense, et la prime qui va avec.
#. column 30: You look to be of able mind and body. Might I interest you in a guildleve?
#. column 31: I sense a certain weakness of both body and mind. I cannot assign a guildleve to one such as yourself. Perhaps good Mother Miounne has a task or two with which you might prove your skills.
#. column 32: The spirits are ever watching, my friend. Prove to them you are worthy of the duty you have been entrusted.
#. column 33: I sense a certain weakness of both body and mind. I cannot assign a guildleve to one such as yourself. Perhaps you might prove your skills on some lesser foes before attempting to take on those which lurk nearby.
#. column 34: You return in one piece, so I can only assume that the spirits approve of your deeds. Allow me to prepare your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:12:0:37"
msgid "And what is this? A little bird tells me that you have dispatched a wanted villain. That would make this bounty yours, as well."
msgstr "А это что? Птичка напела, что вы расправились с разыскиваемым злодеем. Значит, награда за его голову ваша."

#. ja: この辺りの連中からの依頼を、<br>ギルドリーヴとして発行しているぜ。
#. de: Die Leute hier können jede Hilfe gebrauchen, die sie kriegen können. Bist du dabei?
#. fr: <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>Bonsoir<else>Bonjour</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>Bonjour<else>Bonsoir</if></if> aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>. Vous cherchez du travail<nbsp>? J'ai ce qu'il vous faut<nbsp>!
#. column 31: The people of Little Ala Mhigo are in dire need of aid, but only from those with the capacity to give it. <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> will decide whether or not you are worthy. I suggest speaking with <switch $n1><case>him<case>her<case>her</switch> if you ever wish to embark on a levequest.
#. column 32: May you return unharmed.
#. column 33: The people of Little Ala Mhigo are in dire need of aid, but only from those with the capacity to give it. Prove you have that capacity in the field first if you ever wish to embark on one of our levequests.
#. column 34: You appear none the worse for wear. This reward should help lift your spirits.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: As will this bounty for the wanted target you put down. A true menace, that character was.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:13:0:30"
msgid "The people here need any and all help that happens their way. Might you be here to lend your blade?"
msgstr "Здесь всем нужна помощь, какая только найдётся. Не за тем ли вы пришли, чтобы взяться за оружие?"

#. ja: ふむ、仕事を探しているようだが、<br>その実力ではムリというものだ。<br><key>まずは、冒険者ギルドの顔役でもある<br><switch $n1><case>バデロン<case>ミューヌ<case>モモディ</switch>に認められるくらいの<br>腕をつけるんだな。
#. de: Die Bewohner von Klein-Ala Mhigo benötigen dringend Unterstützung. Aber mit einem Grünschnabel ist ihnen nicht geholfen. <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> entscheidet, wer so weit ist und wer nicht. Sprich zuerst mit <switch $n1><case>ihm<case>ihr<case>ihr</switch>.
#. fr: Vous cherchez du travail<nbsp>? Je peux ef<shy>fec<shy>ti<shy>ve<shy>ment vous proposer les mandats des environs, mais vous devez d'abord obtenir la permission auprès de <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>. Continuez à venir en aide aux autres et vos efforts finiront par être récompensés, foi d'Esmond<nbsp>!
#. column 30: The people here need any and all help that happens their way. Might you be here to lend your blade?
#. column 32: May you return unharmed.
#. column 33: The people of Little Ala Mhigo are in dire need of aid, but only from those with the capacity to give it. Prove you have that capacity in the field first if you ever wish to embark on one of our levequests.
#. column 34: You appear none the worse for wear. This reward should help lift your spirits.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: As will this bounty for the wanted target you put down. A true menace, that character was.
#. macro: <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <switch $n1><case>him<case>her<case>her</switch> — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:13:0:31"
msgid "The people of Little Ala Mhigo are in dire need of aid, but only from those with the capacity to give it. <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> will decide whether or not you are worthy. I suggest speaking with <switch $n1><case>him<case>her<case>her</switch> if you ever wish to embark on a levequest."
msgstr "Жителям Малого Ала Миго нужна помощь, но помочь смогут лишь те, кому это по силам. <switch $n1><case>Бадерон Десятипалый<case>Мать Миунне<case>Момоди Моди</switch> решит, достойны ли вы. Хотите взяться за поручение — поговорите с <switch $n1><case>ним<case>ней<case>ней</switch>."

#. ja: 武運を祈ってるぜ。
#. de: Gib gut auf dich acht.
#. fr: Bonne chance à vous, aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>.
#. column 30: The people here need any and all help that happens their way. Might you be here to lend your blade?
#. column 31: The people of Little Ala Mhigo are in dire need of aid, but only from those with the capacity to give it. <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> will decide whether or not you are worthy. I suggest speaking with <switch $n1><case>him<case>her<case>her</switch> if you ever wish to embark on a levequest.
#. column 33: The people of Little Ala Mhigo are in dire need of aid, but only from those with the capacity to give it. Prove you have that capacity in the field first if you ever wish to embark on one of our levequests.
#. column 34: You appear none the worse for wear. This reward should help lift your spirits.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: As will this bounty for the wanted target you put down. A true menace, that character was.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:13:0:32"
msgid "May you return unharmed."
msgstr "Возвращайтесь целым и невредимым."

#. ja: ふむ、仕事を探しているようだが、<br>その実力ではムリというものだ。<br><key>お前さんが、この辺りをうろつく魔物に<br>後れを取らないくらいに、実力をつけたら、<br>いくらでも仕事を斡旋してやるさ。
#. de: Die Bewohner von Klein-Ala Mhigo benötigen dringend Unterstützung. Aber du musst dich erst da draußen beweisen, bevor ich dir einen Freibrief anvertrauen kann.
#. fr: Vous cherchez du travail<nbsp>? Je peux ef<shy>fec<shy>ti<shy>ve<shy>ment vous proposer les mandats des environs, mais vous devez d'abord progresser pour cela.
#. column 30: The people here need any and all help that happens their way. Might you be here to lend your blade?
#. column 31: The people of Little Ala Mhigo are in dire need of aid, but only from those with the capacity to give it. <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> will decide whether or not you are worthy. I suggest speaking with <switch $n1><case>him<case>her<case>her</switch> if you ever wish to embark on a levequest.
#. column 32: May you return unharmed.
#. column 34: You appear none the worse for wear. This reward should help lift your spirits.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: As will this bounty for the wanted target you put down. A true menace, that character was.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:13:0:33"
msgid "The people of Little Ala Mhigo are in dire need of aid, but only from those with the capacity to give it. Prove you have that capacity in the field first if you ever wish to embark on one of our levequests."
msgstr "Жителям Малого Ала Миго нужна помощь, но помочь смогут лишь те, кому это по силам. Сперва докажите в деле, что вы на это способны, и тогда сможете взяться за поручение."

#. ja: おう、お疲れさん。<br>よくやってくれたな……<br>ほら、こいつが報酬だ。取っておきな。
#. de: Du siehst ziemlich mitgenommen aus. Hier, diese Belohnung wird dich aufmuntern.
#. fr: Ça va<nbsp>? Vous semblez éprouvé<if $gn4>e</if>... Tenez, cette récompense devrait vous redonner du baume au cœur. N'hésitez pas à venir me trouver si vous désirez travailler davantage, votre aide sera toujours la bienvenue à Petite Ala Mhigo.
#. column 30: The people here need any and all help that happens their way. Might you be here to lend your blade?
#. column 31: The people of Little Ala Mhigo are in dire need of aid, but only from those with the capacity to give it. <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> will decide whether or not you are worthy. I suggest speaking with <switch $n1><case>him<case>her<case>her</switch> if you ever wish to embark on a levequest.
#. column 32: May you return unharmed.
#. column 33: The people of Little Ala Mhigo are in dire need of aid, but only from those with the capacity to give it. Prove you have that capacity in the field first if you ever wish to embark on one of our levequests.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: As will this bounty for the wanted target you put down. A true menace, that character was.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:13:0:34"
msgid "You appear none the worse for wear. This reward should help lift your spirits."
msgstr "Выглядите вы не слишком измотанным. Вот награда, она поднимет вам настроение."

#. ja: なに、手配中の賞金首を倒しただと！？<br>まったく大した奴だ！　報酬を上乗せするぜ！
#. de: Genau wie das Kopfgeld, das du dir redlich verdient hast.
#. fr: Bravo, c'est l'excellent travail<nbsp>! Les habitants du hameau seront cer<shy>tai<shy>ne<shy>ment ravis d'apprendre que cette créature est désormais hors d'état de nuire. Tenez, voici votre récompense ainsi que la prime de tête<nbsp>!
#. column 30: The people here need any and all help that happens their way. Might you be here to lend your blade?
#. column 31: The people of Little Ala Mhigo are in dire need of aid, but only from those with the capacity to give it. <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> will decide whether or not you are worthy. I suggest speaking with <switch $n1><case>him<case>her<case>her</switch> if you ever wish to embark on a levequest.
#. column 32: May you return unharmed.
#. column 33: The people of Little Ala Mhigo are in dire need of aid, but only from those with the capacity to give it. Prove you have that capacity in the field first if you ever wish to embark on one of our levequests.
#. column 34: You appear none the worse for wear. This reward should help lift your spirits.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:13:0:37"
msgid "As will this bounty for the wanted target you put down. A true menace, that character was."
msgstr "И награда за голову разыскиваемого преступника, которого вы уложили. Он и правда был сущим бедствием."

#. ja: ワインポート近辺での依頼を、<br>ギルドリーヴとして発行しているよ。
#. de: Tut mir aufrichtig leid, aber ich habe leider keinen Wein für dich. Wie wäre es stattdessen mit einem Freibrief?
#. fr: Je suis Aileen, responsable des mandats de guilde à Port-aux-Vins.
#. column 31: Let me guess─you journeyed all the way to Wineport looking for a nice drop of our finest red, before realizing your purse was naught but a den of lint and pebbles, and now you seek employment. Well, while there is work to be had, you shall be getting none of it until I have received word from <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> regarding your commitment to the Adventurers' Guild.
#. column 32: The wine will be waiting when you return.
#. column 33: Let me guess─you journeyed all the way to Wineport looking for a nice drop of our finest red, before realizing your purse was naught but a den of lint and pebbles, and now you seek employment. Well, while there is work to be had, you shall be getting none of it until you have proven yourself able to bear the burden a harsh environ such as this can present.
#. column 34: You continue to prove yourself a competent...and sober choice for our clients. Keep up the fine work, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: That you can find time to slay wanted targets while completing leve objectives will only help to solidify you as <i>the</i> adventurer to choose when needing a task handled promptly and properly. Here is the bounty for this outing's find.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:14:0:30"
msgid "Back looking for work to fund that wine habit, are we?"
msgstr "Опять ищете работу, чтобы оплатить привычку к вину?"

#. ja: 私の役目は、この近辺での依頼を、<br>「ギルドリーヴ」として発行することさ。<br><br>だけど、まずは冒険者ギルドの顔役、<br><switch $n1><case>バデロン<case>ミューヌ<case>モモディ</switch>さんから紹介を受けてきてくれるかい？<br>実力者にこそ、任せたい仕事ばかりだからね。
#. de: Du hast gestern Abend wohl zu viel von unserem guten Wein getrunken! Um Freibriefe annehmen zu können, reicht angetrunkener Mut leider nicht aus. Geh zu <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>, wenn du wieder nüchtern bist, <switch $n1><case>er<case>sie<case>sie</switch> kann dir bestimmt weiterhelfen.
#. fr: Mon rôle est de confier les requêtes des habitants du coin aux aventuriers de passage. Ah, je vois que tu es intéressé<if $gn4>e</if><nbsp>? Dans ce cas, tu vas d'abord devoir obtenir une re<shy>com<shy>man<shy>da<shy>tion de la part de <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>.
#. column 30: Back looking for work to fund that wine habit, are we?
#. column 32: The wine will be waiting when you return.
#. column 33: Let me guess─you journeyed all the way to Wineport looking for a nice drop of our finest red, before realizing your purse was naught but a den of lint and pebbles, and now you seek employment. Well, while there is work to be had, you shall be getting none of it until you have proven yourself able to bear the burden a harsh environ such as this can present.
#. column 34: You continue to prove yourself a competent...and sober choice for our clients. Keep up the fine work, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>.
