msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:14:0:37"
msgid "That you can find time to slay wanted targets while completing leve objectives will only help to solidify you as <i>the</i> adventurer to choose when needing a task handled promptly and properly. Here is the bounty for this outing's find."
msgstr "Успевать выполнять поручения и ещё расправляться с разыскиваемыми преступниками — вот что делает вас <i>тем самым</i> искателем приключений, которого зовут, когда дело нужно сделать быстро и как следует. Вот награда за голову, которую вы принесли."

#. ja: 私は、ここアドネール占星台近辺での依頼を<br>「ギルドリーヴ」として発行しております。
#. de: Freibriefe erhalten von mir nur die weitsichtigsten aller Abenteurer.
#. fr: Bien le <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>bonsoir<else>bonjour</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>bonjour<else>bonsoir</if></if>, aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>. C'est moi qui m'occupe des mandats, à l'Observatoire.
#. column 31: I sense you have an interest in serving the region. Yet, though even a blind man could see your zeal, I am afraid I must turn you away. You see, my registers do not include your name, and only a recommendation from <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> of the Adventurers' Guild in <switch $n1><case>Limsa Lominsa<case>New Gridania<case>Ul'dah</switch> can see your name added.
#. column 32: May the Fury give you strength.
#. column 33: I sense you have an interest in serving the region. Yet, though even a blind man could see your zeal, I am afraid I must turn you away. You see, I could not, in good conscience, send a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your inexperience into the field, knowing you might never return.
#. column 34: The levewatches spoke once again of your skill and valor. Your service to Ishgard is a blessing from the Fury Herself.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And I see She gave you strength to overcome additional hardship. Your claim on this bounty is undeniable. It has truly been an honor, <if $gn4>madam<else>sir</if>.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:15:0:30"
msgid "Have you further interest in aiding the region through levequests?"
msgstr "Вы ещё хотите помогать здешним жителям, выполняя поручения?"

#. ja: 何やらお仕事を探しておられる様子……<br>確かに私は、「ギルドリーヴ」の発行を<br>その務めとしております。<br>ですが、まずは冒険者ギルドの顔役、<br><switch $n1><case>バデロン<case>ミューヌ<case>モモディ</switch>さんから紹介を受けてください。<br>相応の実力が必要な仕事ですから……。
#. de: Du täuschst Weitsicht vor, wo keine ist. Ich kann deiner Forderung nach einem Freibrief deshalb leider nicht entsprechen. Kehre zur Aben<shy>teurer<shy>gilde zurück und sprich mit <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>. Dort wirst du erfahren, was als nächstes zu tun ist.
#. fr: Vous cherchez du travail, n'est-ce pas<nbsp>? Vous vous adressez à la bonne personne, mais je ne peux malheureusement pas vous en confier tant que vous n'avez pas de re<shy>com<shy>man<shy>da<shy>tion de <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>.
#. column 30: Have you further interest in aiding the region through levequests?
#. column 32: May the Fury give you strength.
#. column 33: I sense you have an interest in serving the region. Yet, though even a blind man could see your zeal, I am afraid I must turn you away. You see, I could not, in good conscience, send a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your inexperience into the field, knowing you might never return.
#. column 34: The levewatches spoke once again of your skill and valor. Your service to Ishgard is a blessing from the Fury Herself.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And I see She gave you strength to overcome additional hardship. Your claim on this bounty is undeniable. It has truly been an honor, <if $gn4>madam<else>sir</if>.
#. macro: <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <switch $n1><case>Limsa Lominsa<case>New Gridania<case>Ul'dah</switch> — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:15:0:31"
msgid "I sense you have an interest in serving the region. Yet, though even a blind man could see your zeal, I am afraid I must turn you away. You see, my registers do not include your name, and only a recommendation from <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> of the Adventurers' Guild in <switch $n1><case>Limsa Lominsa<case>New Gridania<case>Ul'dah</switch> can see your name added."
msgstr "Похоже, вы хотите послужить этим краям. Это похвально! Но как бы ни был заметен ваш пыл, вынужден вам отказать. Видите ли, вашего имени нет в моих записях, а внести его туда может лишь рекомендация от <switch $n1><case>Бадерона Десятипалого<case>Матери Миунне<case>Момоди Моди</switch> из гильдии искателей приключений в <switch $n1><case>Лимсе Ломинсе<case>Новой Гридании<case>Уль'де</switch>."

#. ja: 任務の成功と、貴方の無事を祈っております。<br>どうかご武運を……。
#. de: Möge dich deine Weitsicht zum Erfolg führen!
#. fr: J'espère vous voir revenir de votre mission sain<if $gn4>e et sauve<else> et sauf</if>, aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>.
#. column 30: Have you further interest in aiding the region through levequests?
#. column 31: I sense you have an interest in serving the region. Yet, though even a blind man could see your zeal, I am afraid I must turn you away. You see, my registers do not include your name, and only a recommendation from <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> of the Adventurers' Guild in <switch $n1><case>Limsa Lominsa<case>New Gridania<case>Ul'dah</switch> can see your name added.
#. column 33: I sense you have an interest in serving the region. Yet, though even a blind man could see your zeal, I am afraid I must turn you away. You see, I could not, in good conscience, send a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your inexperience into the field, knowing you might never return.
#. column 34: The levewatches spoke once again of your skill and valor. Your service to Ishgard is a blessing from the Fury Herself.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And I see She gave you strength to overcome additional hardship. Your claim on this bounty is undeniable. It has truly been an honor, <if $gn4>madam<else>sir</if>.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:15:0:32"
msgid "May the Fury give you strength."
msgstr "Пусть Фурия придаст вам сил."

#. ja: 何やらお仕事を探しておられる様子……<br>確かに私は、「ギルドリーヴ」の発行を<br>その務めとしております。<br>ですが、まずは経験を積んできてください。<br>相応の実力が必要な仕事ですから……。
#. de: Du täuschst Weitsicht vor, wo keine ist. Ich kann deiner Forderung nach einem Freibrief deshalb leider nicht entsprechen. Versuche dich zunächst an schwächeren Gegnern, bevor du erneut an mich herantrittst.
#. fr: Vous cherchez du travail, n'est-ce pas<nbsp>? Vous vous adressez à la bonne personne, mais je ne peux malheureusement pas vous en confier pour le moment. Allez donc vous entraîner avant de revenir me parler.
#. column 30: Have you further interest in aiding the region through levequests?
#. column 31: I sense you have an interest in serving the region. Yet, though even a blind man could see your zeal, I am afraid I must turn you away. You see, my registers do not include your name, and only a recommendation from <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> of the Adventurers' Guild in <switch $n1><case>Limsa Lominsa<case>New Gridania<case>Ul'dah</switch> can see your name added.
#. column 32: May the Fury give you strength.
#. column 34: The levewatches spoke once again of your skill and valor. Your service to Ishgard is a blessing from the Fury Herself.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And I see She gave you strength to overcome additional hardship. Your claim on this bounty is undeniable. It has truly been an honor, <if $gn4>madam<else>sir</if>.
#. macro: <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:15:0:33"
msgid "I sense you have an interest in serving the region. Yet, though even a blind man could see your zeal, I am afraid I must turn you away. You see, I could not, in good conscience, send a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your inexperience into the field, knowing you might never return."
msgstr "Вы рветесь послужить этим краям. Это похвально! Но как бы ни был заметен ваш пыл, вынужден вам отказать. Видите ли, я не могу с чистой совестью отправить такого неопытного <if $gn4>человека<else>человека</if> в опасное место, где вы можете не вернуться."

#. ja: 貴方を信じてお待ちしておりました。<br>それでは働きに相応しい報酬を……。<br>依頼人の方も、さぞお喜びになるでしょう。
#. de: Ich war während deiner Abwesenheit so weitsichtig und habe die im Erfolgsfall anstehende Belohnung bereits vorbereitet.
#. fr: Je n'ai jamais douté que vous réussiriez. Veuillez accepter cette récompense de la part du client.
#. column 30: Have you further interest in aiding the region through levequests?
#. column 31: I sense you have an interest in serving the region. Yet, though even a blind man could see your zeal, I am afraid I must turn you away. You see, my registers do not include your name, and only a recommendation from <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> of the Adventurers' Guild in <switch $n1><case>Limsa Lominsa<case>New Gridania<case>Ul'dah</switch> can see your name added.
#. column 32: May the Fury give you strength.
#. column 33: I sense you have an interest in serving the region. Yet, though even a blind man could see your zeal, I am afraid I must turn you away. You see, I could not, in good conscience, send a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your inexperience into the field, knowing you might never return.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And I see She gave you strength to overcome additional hardship. Your claim on this bounty is undeniable. It has truly been an honor, <if $gn4>madam<else>sir</if>.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:15:0:34"
msgid "The levewatches spoke once again of your skill and valor. Your service to Ishgard is a blessing from the Fury Herself."
msgstr "Наблюдатели вновь отметили вашу сноровку и отвагу. Сама Фурия благословляет вашу службу Ишгарду."

#. ja: ですが、賞金首まで仕留めるなど、予想以上！<br>これは報酬を増やさねばなりませんね。
#. de: Außerdem hast du anscheinend sehr gut vorausgeplant und dadurch gleichzeitig auch die Bedingungen für den Erhalt des Kopfgeldes erfüllen können. Das nenne ich wahre Weitsicht!
#. fr: Mais je vois que vous avez également abattu une créature recherchée<nbsp>! Prenez aussi ce supplément, je vous prie.
#. column 30: Have you further interest in aiding the region through levequests?
#. column 31: I sense you have an interest in serving the region. Yet, though even a blind man could see your zeal, I am afraid I must turn you away. You see, my registers do not include your name, and only a recommendation from <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> of the Adventurers' Guild in <switch $n1><case>Limsa Lominsa<case>New Gridania<case>Ul'dah</switch> can see your name added.
#. column 32: May the Fury give you strength.
#. column 33: I sense you have an interest in serving the region. Yet, though even a blind man could see your zeal, I am afraid I must turn you away. You see, I could not, in good conscience, send a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your inexperience into the field, knowing you might never return.
#. column 34: The levewatches spoke once again of your skill and valor. Your service to Ishgard is a blessing from the Fury Herself.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. macro: <if $gn4>madam<else>sir</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:15:0:37"
msgid "And I see She gave you strength to overcome additional hardship. Your claim on this bounty is undeniable. It has truly been an honor, <if $gn4>madam<else>sir</if>."
msgstr "Вижу, Фурия дала вам сил преодолеть и это испытание. Награда за голову ваша, тут никаких сомнений. Для меня было честью служить вам, <if $gn4>сударыня<else>сударь</if>."

#. ja: 私は、冒険者ギルドに属する者。<br>ホワイトブリム前哨地近辺における<br>「ギルドリーヴ」の発行業務を担当しておる。
#. de: Hier an der Weißenfels-Front wimmelt es nur so von Drachen und anderen höchst gefährlichen Monstern. Sei also gewarnt - unsere Freibriefe sind nichts für Schwächlinge.
#. fr: La guilde des aventuriers m'a envoyé au poste de L'Arête blanche pour m'occuper des mandats de guilde.
#. column 31: Greetings, adventurer. How might I know you are an adventurer and not of some other noble profession? Why that is simple. We levemetes serve the Adventurers' Guild and are trained to distinguish diamonds from debris...and while you are most certainly a gem, I only put my trust in those who have been properly appraised by <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>.
#. column 32: As the locals would say, may the Fury give you strength and all that.
#. column 33: Greetings, adventurer. How might I know you are an adventurer and not of some other noble profession? Why that is simple. We levemetes serve the Adventurers' Guild and are trained to distinguish diamonds from debris...and while you are most certainly a gem, you could use a few more turns on the grinder...for lack of a better metaphor.
#. column 34: Another job well done, adventurer. You do not mind me calling you by that moniker, do you?
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Why, who other than an adventurer would have been able to slay a wanted target <i>in addition</i> to completing <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> levequest duties? The bounty is yours!
#. macro: <if $gn4>she<else>he</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:16:0:30"
msgid "Ah, <if $gn4>she<else>he</if>-who-is-not-an-adventurer. Or perhaps is. Have you come for a leve, by chance?"
msgstr "А, <if $gn4>та<else>тот</if>, кто не искатель приключений... или всё-таки искатель? Вы случайно не за поручением?"

#. ja: 私は、冒険者ギルドに属する者。<br>ホワイトブリム前哨地近辺における<br>「ギルドリーヴ」の発行業務を担当しておる。<br>だが、まずはギルドの顔役たる<br><switch $n1><case>バデロン氏<case>ミューヌ女史<case>モモディ女史</switch>からの紹介を受けて頂きたい。<br>任務は信頼のおける者に、任せたいのでな。
#. de: Du kommst an die Weißenfels-Front und siehst aus, als könntest du es noch nicht einmal mit einer Schneemaus aufnehmen. Sprich lieber vorher noch mal mit <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>, bevor du dich hier ins Verderben stürzt.
#. fr: C'est un bon moyen de vous enrichir en aidant les habitants, vous savez<nbsp>? En revanche, je dois vous demander d'obtenir une re<shy>com<shy>man<shy>da<shy>tion de la part de <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> avant de pouvoir vous confier du travail. Question de confiance, tout simplement.
#. column 30: Ah, <if $gn4>she<else>he</if>-who-is-not-an-adventurer. Or perhaps is. Have you come for a leve, by chance?
#. column 32: As the locals would say, may the Fury give you strength and all that.
#. column 33: Greetings, adventurer. How might I know you are an adventurer and not of some other noble profession? Why that is simple. We levemetes serve the Adventurers' Guild and are trained to distinguish diamonds from debris...and while you are most certainly a gem, you could use a few more turns on the grinder...for lack of a better metaphor.
#. column 34: Another job well done, adventurer. You do not mind me calling you by that moniker, do you?
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Why, who other than an adventurer would have been able to slay a wanted target <i>in addition</i> to completing <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> levequest duties? The bounty is yours!
#. macro: <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:16:0:31"
msgid "Greetings, adventurer. How might I know you are an adventurer and not of some other noble profession? Why that is simple. We levemetes serve the Adventurers' Guild and are trained to distinguish diamonds from debris...and while you are most certainly a gem, I only put my trust in those who have been properly appraised by <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>."
msgstr "Приветствую, искатель приключений. Как понять, что вы искатель, а не представитель другой почтенной профессии? Всё просто. Мы, распорядители поручений, служим гильдии искателей приключений и умеем отличать алмазы от булыжников... Вы, несомненно, драгоценный камень, но я доверяю лишь тем, чьи способности проверили <switch $n1><case>Бадерон Десятипалый<case>Мать Миунне<case>Момоди Моди</switch>."

#. ja: 任務の成功を祈っておる。<br>お主に、戦神ハルオーネの加護あらんことを……。
#. de: Halone, die Göttin des Krieges, soll dich auf deinen Abenteuern beschützen!
#. fr: Restez sur vos gardes, et tout devrait bien se passer. Que la Déesse Halone veille sur vous.
#. column 30: Ah, <if $gn4>she<else>he</if>-who-is-not-an-adventurer. Or perhaps is. Have you come for a leve, by chance?
#. column 31: Greetings, adventurer. How might I know you are an adventurer and not of some other noble profession? Why that is simple. We levemetes serve the Adventurers' Guild and are trained to distinguish diamonds from debris...and while you are most certainly a gem, I only put my trust in those who have been properly appraised by <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>.
#. column 33: Greetings, adventurer. How might I know you are an adventurer and not of some other noble profession? Why that is simple. We levemetes serve the Adventurers' Guild and are trained to distinguish diamonds from debris...and while you are most certainly a gem, you could use a few more turns on the grinder...for lack of a better metaphor.
#. column 34: Another job well done, adventurer. You do not mind me calling you by that moniker, do you?
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Why, who other than an adventurer would have been able to slay a wanted target <i>in addition</i> to completing <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> levequest duties? The bounty is yours!
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:16:0:32"
msgid "As the locals would say, may the Fury give you strength and all that."
msgstr "Как здесь говорят, пусть Фурия придаст вам сил и всё такое."

#. ja: 私は、冒険者ギルドに属する者。<br>ホワイトブリム前哨地近辺における<br>「ギルドリーヴ」の発行業務を担当しておる。<br>だが、残念ながらお主には、<br>「ギルドリーヴ」を発行することはできん。<br>もう少し経験を積んでからまいられよ。
#. de: Du kommst an die Weißenfels-Front und siehst aus, als könntest du es noch nicht einmal mit einer Schneemaus aufnehmen. Wenn ich es mir recht überlege, wäre sie im Moment wohl der passendste Gegner für dich. Komm wieder, wenn du erfahrener bist.
#. fr: C'est un bon moyen de vous enrichir en aidant les habitants, vous savez<nbsp>? En revanche, je dois vous demander d'acquérir davantage d'expérience avant de vous confier du travail. Question de confiance, tout simplement.
#. column 30: Ah, <if $gn4>she<else>he</if>-who-is-not-an-adventurer. Or perhaps is. Have you come for a leve, by chance?
#. column 31: Greetings, adventurer. How might I know you are an adventurer and not of some other noble profession? Why that is simple. We levemetes serve the Adventurers' Guild and are trained to distinguish diamonds from debris...and while you are most certainly a gem, I only put my trust in those who have been properly appraised by <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>.
#. column 32: As the locals would say, may the Fury give you strength and all that.
#. column 34: Another job well done, adventurer. You do not mind me calling you by that moniker, do you?
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Why, who other than an adventurer would have been able to slay a wanted target <i>in addition</i> to completing <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> levequest duties? The bounty is yours!
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:16:0:33"
msgid "Greetings, adventurer. How might I know you are an adventurer and not of some other noble profession? Why that is simple. We levemetes serve the Adventurers' Guild and are trained to distinguish diamonds from debris...and while you are most certainly a gem, you could use a few more turns on the grinder...for lack of a better metaphor."
msgstr "Приветствую, искатель приключений. Как понять, что вы искатель, а не представитель другой почтенной профессии? Всё просто. Мы, распорядители поручений, служим гильдии искателей приключений и умеем отличать алмазы от булыжников... Вы, несомненно, драгоценный камень, но вам бы ещё немного шлифовки... если позволите такое сравнение."

#. ja: さすがは熟練の冒険者。<br>その見事な働きに対し、報酬を支払おう。<br>依頼人たちも、満足することであろうな。
#. de: Ich habe es dir vom ersten Moment an angesehen. Du könntest es bestimmt auch mit zehn Drachen gleichzeitig aufnehmen! Hier ist deine Belohnung.
#. fr: Je n'en attendais pas moins d'un<if $gn4>e aventurière<else> aventurier</if> comme vous. C'est notre client qui va être content<nbsp>! Tenez, votre récompense.
#. column 30: Ah, <if $gn4>she<else>he</if>-who-is-not-an-adventurer. Or perhaps is. Have you come for a leve, by chance?
#. column 31: Greetings, adventurer. How might I know you are an adventurer and not of some other noble profession? Why that is simple. We levemetes serve the Adventurers' Guild and are trained to distinguish diamonds from debris...and while you are most certainly a gem, I only put my trust in those who have been properly appraised by <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>.
#. column 32: As the locals would say, may the Fury give you strength and all that.
#. column 33: Greetings, adventurer. How might I know you are an adventurer and not of some other noble profession? Why that is simple. We levemetes serve the Adventurers' Guild and are trained to distinguish diamonds from debris...and while you are most certainly a gem, you could use a few more turns on the grinder...for lack of a better metaphor.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Why, who other than an adventurer would have been able to slay a wanted target <i>in addition</i> to completing <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> levequest duties? The bounty is yours!
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:16:0:34"
msgid "Another job well done, adventurer. You do not mind me calling you by that moniker, do you?"
msgstr "Ещё одно дело сделано на славу, искатель приключений. Не возражаете, если я так вас называю?"

#. ja: そして、任務の達成に加え、<br>賞金首まで仕留めるという功績を挙げるとは。<br>報酬を上乗せし、その働きに応えるとしよう。
#. de: Das Kopfgeld kommt natürlich noch obendrauf. Ich habe nichts anderes als einen vollen Erfolg von dir erwartet. Gut gemacht.
#. fr: Et ce n'est pas tout<nbsp>! Comme vous avez abattu une créature recherchée, vous avez également droit à ce supplément. Fé<shy>li<shy>ci<shy>ta<shy>tions<nbsp>!
#. column 30: Ah, <if $gn4>she<else>he</if>-who-is-not-an-adventurer. Or perhaps is. Have you come for a leve, by chance?
#. column 31: Greetings, adventurer. How might I know you are an adventurer and not of some other noble profession? Why that is simple. We levemetes serve the Adventurers' Guild and are trained to distinguish diamonds from debris...and while you are most certainly a gem, I only put my trust in those who have been properly appraised by <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>.
#. column 32: As the locals would say, may the Fury give you strength and all that.
#. column 33: Greetings, adventurer. How might I know you are an adventurer and not of some other noble profession? Why that is simple. We levemetes serve the Adventurers' Guild and are trained to distinguish diamonds from debris...and while you are most certainly a gem, you could use a few more turns on the grinder...for lack of a better metaphor.
#. column 34: Another job well done, adventurer. You do not mind me calling you by that moniker, do you?
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
