#. macro: <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:18:0:31"
msgid "\\<sigh> Why anyone would <i>choose</i> to come to a place such as th─ Ah, you there! You look to be a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action. Might I suggest that before entertaining any grand ideas about saving Bluefog from the fetters of evil that you “act” upon my suggestion of gaining the trust of Adventurers' Guild proprietor <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>? Then, I might be able to accommodate your whims."
msgstr "\\<вздыхает> И зачем только люди <i>добровольно</i> едут в такие места─ А, вы! На вид вы <if $gn4>девушка<else>парень</if> деятельная. Только вот прежде чем строить грандиозные планы по спасению Синего Тумана от зла, лучше бы вы «действовали» по моему совету и заслужили доверие хозяина Гильдии искателей приключений <switch $n1><case>Бадерона Десятипалого<case>матушки Мионне<case>Момоди Моди</switch>. Тогда, возможно, я и исполню ваши прихоти."

#. ja: それじゃあ、任務を頑張ってくれよな。<br>報酬の準備をしておくからさ。
#. de: Gib dein Bestes! Ich bin sicher, dass du erfolgreich zurückkehren wirst.
#. fr: Bon, tout m'a l'air en ordre... C'est à toi de jouer, maintenant<nbsp>!
#. column 30: \<sigh> What did I ever do to deserve this post─ Ah, you there! I recall you as a regular <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action. Might I interest you in another guildleve?
#. column 31: \<sigh> Why anyone would <i>choose</i> to come to a place such as th─ Ah, you there! You look to be a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action. Might I suggest that before entertaining any grand ideas about saving Bluefog from the fetters of evil that you “act” upon my suggestion of gaining the trust of Adventurers' Guild proprietor <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>? Then, I might be able to accommodate your whims.
#. column 33: \<sigh> Why anyone would <i>choose</i> to come to a place such as th─ Ah, you there! You look to be a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action... Though, upon closer inspection, you do not appear to have <i>seen</i> much of the stuff. My leves require those who undertake them to put the “act” in “action.” I cannot offer them to one not even ready to spell “act,” let alone...<i>act</i> act.
#. column 34: The <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action has returned with another leve under <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> belt! So, then. Are you ready to be <i>richly</i> recompensed for services rendered?
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And what is this? The levewatch informs me that you have slain a wanted target. Huzzah and hurrah. The bounty is claimed!
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:18:0:32"
msgid "Remember, if you die, you cannot claim your reward! Good luck!"
msgstr "Помните: погибнете — награду не получите! Удачи!"

#. ja: キャンプ・ブルーフォグ周辺に関連した依頼を、<br>「ギルドリーヴ」として発行するのが僕の役目さ。<br><br>だけど、君には少しばかり経験が足りないようだ。<br>この辺りの魔物を、楽々と倒せるくらいの<br>実力者に仕事を任せたいからね。
#. de: Ich würde dir gerne einen der Freibriefe anvertrauen, aber ich befürchte leider, dass du noch nicht erfahren genug bist. Entschuldige, ist nicht persönlich gemeint.
#. fr: Tu cherches quelque chose à faire, pas vrai<nbsp>? Désolé, mais je ne peux pas te confier de mandat pour le moment. Tu dois t'aguerrir davantage<nbsp>! C'est du travail sérieux, tu comprends<nbsp>?
#. column 30: \<sigh> What did I ever do to deserve this post─ Ah, you there! I recall you as a regular <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action. Might I interest you in another guildleve?
#. column 31: \<sigh> Why anyone would <i>choose</i> to come to a place such as th─ Ah, you there! You look to be a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action. Might I suggest that before entertaining any grand ideas about saving Bluefog from the fetters of evil that you “act” upon my suggestion of gaining the trust of Adventurers' Guild proprietor <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>? Then, I might be able to accommodate your whims.
#. column 32: Remember, if you die, you cannot claim your reward! Good luck!
#. column 34: The <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action has returned with another leve under <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> belt! So, then. Are you ready to be <i>richly</i> recompensed for services rendered?
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And what is this? The levewatch informs me that you have slain a wanted target. Huzzah and hurrah. The bounty is claimed!
