msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:18:0:33"
msgid "\\<sigh> Why anyone would <i>choose</i> to come to a place such as th─ Ah, you there! You look to be a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action... Though, upon closer inspection, you do not appear to have <i>seen</i> much of the stuff. My leves require those who undertake them to put the “act” in “action.” I cannot offer them to one not even ready to spell “act,” let alone...<i>act</i> act."
msgstr "\\<вздыхает> И зачем только люди <i>добровольно</i> едут в такие места─ А, вы! На вид вы <if $gn4>девушка<else>парень</if> деятельная... Хотя, если присмотреться, приключений вы пока почти не видали. За мои поручения берутся те, кто умеет не только говорить, но и <i>действовать</i>. А вам я их поручить не могу: вы ещё даже слова «дело» не освоили, не то что... <i>делать</i> дела."

#. ja: 今回の任務は成功……っと。<br>冒険者ギルドに提出する記録もつけたことだし、<br>お待ちかねの報酬といこうか。
#. de: Ich bin von deinem fabelhaften Können begeistert. Hier ist dein verdienter Lohn!
#. fr: Tu as brillament rempli ta mission. Je vais te récompenser sans plus attendre.
#. column 30: \<sigh> What did I ever do to deserve this post─ Ah, you there! I recall you as a regular <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action. Might I interest you in another guildleve?
#. column 31: \<sigh> Why anyone would <i>choose</i> to come to a place such as th─ Ah, you there! You look to be a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action. Might I suggest that before entertaining any grand ideas about saving Bluefog from the fetters of evil that you “act” upon my suggestion of gaining the trust of Adventurers' Guild proprietor <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>? Then, I might be able to accommodate your whims.
#. column 32: Remember, if you die, you cannot claim your reward! Good luck!
#. column 33: \<sigh> Why anyone would <i>choose</i> to come to a place such as th─ Ah, you there! You look to be a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action... Though, upon closer inspection, you do not appear to have <i>seen</i> much of the stuff. My leves require those who undertake them to put the “act” in “action.” I cannot offer them to one not even ready to spell “act,” let alone...<i>act</i> act.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And what is this? The levewatch informs me that you have slain a wanted target. Huzzah and hurrah. The bounty is claimed!
#. macro: <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:18:0:34"
msgid "The <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action has returned with another leve under <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> belt! So, then. Are you ready to be <i>richly</i> recompensed for services rendered?"
msgstr "<if $gn4>Девушка<else>Парень</if> при деле вернулась с ещё одним поручением за плечами! Ну что, готовы получить <i>щедрую</i> плату за свои труды?"

#. ja: 今回の任務は大成功……っと。<br>任務の達成に加えて、賞金首も倒したんだ。<br>ギルドの規定通り、ボーナスを支給しておくよ。
#. de: Und an das Kopfgeld hast du natürlich auch gedacht und alles wie gewünscht erledigt. Wunderbar.
#. fr: Oh, attends un peu... Tu as carrément réussi à abattre une créature recherchée<nbsp>!? Ça alors<nbsp>! Tiens, voilà la paye qui correspond. Et merci encore<nbsp>!
#. column 30: \<sigh> What did I ever do to deserve this post─ Ah, you there! I recall you as a regular <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action. Might I interest you in another guildleve?
#. column 31: \<sigh> Why anyone would <i>choose</i> to come to a place such as th─ Ah, you there! You look to be a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action. Might I suggest that before entertaining any grand ideas about saving Bluefog from the fetters of evil that you “act” upon my suggestion of gaining the trust of Adventurers' Guild proprietor <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>? Then, I might be able to accommodate your whims.
#. column 32: Remember, if you die, you cannot claim your reward! Good luck!
#. column 33: \<sigh> Why anyone would <i>choose</i> to come to a place such as th─ Ah, you there! You look to be a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action... Though, upon closer inspection, you do not appear to have <i>seen</i> much of the stuff. My leves require those who undertake them to put the “act” in “action.” I cannot offer them to one not even ready to spell “act,” let alone...<i>act</i> act.
#. column 34: The <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of action has returned with another leve under <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> belt! So, then. Are you ready to be <i>richly</i> recompensed for services rendered?
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:18:0:37"
msgid "And what is this? The levewatch informs me that you have slain a wanted target. Huzzah and hurrah. The bounty is claimed!"
msgstr "А это ещё что? Смотритель поручений докладывает, что вы одолели разыскиваемую цель. Ура да здравствует! Награда за голову ваша!"

#. ja: スコーピオン交易所周辺に関連した依頼を<br>ギルドリーヴとして発行しているよ。
#. de: Ich vergebe Freibriefe für die Umgebung vom Skorpionen-Treff. Willst du dich nicht daran versuchen?
#. fr: Bien le <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>bonsoir<else>bonjour</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>bonjour<else>bonsoir</if></if> aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>. J'ai en ma possession divers mandats de guilde, que je pourrai vous proposer si vous êtes intéressé<if $gn4>e</if>.
#. column 31: Western Thanalan needs your help, but I've seen more worthy tumbleweeds roll through the Crossing. You should climb your way back to the Adventurers' Guild and make yourself known to the guildmaster. Once I have the approval of the guild, then I might be able to accommodate you with a leve or two.
#. column 32: Good luck and godsspeed!
#. column 33: Western Thanalan needs your help, but I've seen more worthy tumbleweeds roll through the Crossing. You should step out from behind your mummy's frillies and bloody that weapon of yours. Once I find you fit, then I might consider entrusting you with a leve or two.
#. column 34: I see you are still with us in the realm of Nald. Thal will be disappointed, but He always is. Here is your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And with it, the bounty you earned for slaying that wanted target. Impressive work, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. Quite impressive.
#. macro: <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:19:0:30"
msgid "Western Thanalan needs your help. Are you <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> enough to give it?"
msgstr "Западный Таналан нуждается в вашей помощи. Хватит ли у вас духу взяться за дело?"

#. ja: 仕事を探してるってのかい？<br>確かに、アタシらはこの辺から寄せられた依頼を<br>「ギルドリーヴ」として発行しているさ。<br>だけど、まずは冒険者ギルドの顔役、<br><switch $n1><case>バデロン<case>ミューヌ<case>モモディ</switch>さんから紹介を受けてほしいもんだね。<br>誰でもいいって仕事なわけじゃないのさ。
#. de: Suchst du Arbeit? Viele Bewohner dieser Gegend, die ein Problem haben, kommen damit zu uns. Wir stellen dann einen Freibrief aus. Natürlich vergeben wir den nicht an jeden x-Beliebigen. Wir nehmen nur Leute, die uns von <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> empfohlen wurden. Geh doch noch einmal bei der Aben<shy>teurer<shy>gilde vorbei.
#. fr: Pardon<nbsp>? Vous cherchez du travail, vous dites<nbsp>? Hmm... Je vous aurais bien proposé des mandats de guilde, mais vous n'avez pas encore prouvé votre valeur à <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>... Revenez me voir plus tard.
#. column 30: Western Thanalan needs your help. Are you <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> enough to give it?
#. column 32: Good luck and godsspeed!
#. column 33: Western Thanalan needs your help, but I've seen more worthy tumbleweeds roll through the Crossing. You should step out from behind your mummy's frillies and bloody that weapon of yours. Once I find you fit, then I might consider entrusting you with a leve or two.
#. column 34: I see you are still with us in the realm of Nald. Thal will be disappointed, but He always is. Here is your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And with it, the bounty you earned for slaying that wanted target. Impressive work, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. Quite impressive.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:19:0:31"
msgid "Western Thanalan needs your help, but I've seen more worthy tumbleweeds roll through the Crossing. You should climb your way back to the Adventurers' Guild and make yourself known to the guildmaster. Once I have the approval of the guild, then I might be able to accommodate you with a leve or two."
msgstr "Западному Таналану нужна помощь, а я тут повидал перекати-поле и посолиднее вас. Возвращайтесь в Гильдию искателей приключений, познакомьтесь с её главой и получите его одобрение. Тогда, может, и поручение найдётся."

#. ja: 任務の成功を信じてるよ。<br>さあ、行っといで！
#. de: Ich bin mir sicher, dass du den Freibrief ordnungsgemäß erfüllst. Also los!
#. fr: Tout est en règle, vous pouvez y aller. J'espère que la chance vous sourira.
#. column 30: Western Thanalan needs your help. Are you <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> enough to give it?
#. column 31: Western Thanalan needs your help, but I've seen more worthy tumbleweeds roll through the Crossing. You should climb your way back to the Adventurers' Guild and make yourself known to the guildmaster. Once I have the approval of the guild, then I might be able to accommodate you with a leve or two.
#. column 33: Western Thanalan needs your help, but I've seen more worthy tumbleweeds roll through the Crossing. You should step out from behind your mummy's frillies and bloody that weapon of yours. Once I find you fit, then I might consider entrusting you with a leve or two.
#. column 34: I see you are still with us in the realm of Nald. Thal will be disappointed, but He always is. Here is your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And with it, the bounty you earned for slaying that wanted target. Impressive work, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. Quite impressive.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:19:0:32"
msgid "Good luck and godsspeed!"
msgstr "Удачи, и пусть боги хранят вас!"

#. ja: 仕事を探してるってのかい？<br>確かに、アタシらはこの辺から寄せられた依頼を<br>「ギルドリーヴ」として発行しているさ。<br>だけど、実力不足の奴には任せられないね。<br>相応の腕ってやつを、身に着けたら<br>仕事を回させてもらうよ。
#. de: Suchst du Arbeit? Viele Bewohner dieser Gegend, die ein Problem haben, kommen damit zu uns. Wir stellen dann einen Freibrief aus. Natürlich vergeben wir den nicht an jeden x-Beliebigen. Nur wer genug Erfahrung vorweisen kann, wird mit einem Auftrag bedacht.
#. fr: Pardon<nbsp>? Vous cherchez du travail, vous dites<nbsp>? Je suis désolée, mais je ne suis pas autorisée à proposer des mandats aux aventuriers débutants. Revenez me voir quand vous serez capable de tuer autre chose que des marmottes et des musaraignes.
#. column 30: Western Thanalan needs your help. Are you <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> enough to give it?
#. column 31: Western Thanalan needs your help, but I've seen more worthy tumbleweeds roll through the Crossing. You should climb your way back to the Adventurers' Guild and make yourself known to the guildmaster. Once I have the approval of the guild, then I might be able to accommodate you with a leve or two.
#. column 32: Good luck and godsspeed!
#. column 34: I see you are still with us in the realm of Nald. Thal will be disappointed, but He always is. Here is your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And with it, the bounty you earned for slaying that wanted target. Impressive work, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. Quite impressive.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:19:0:33"
msgid "Western Thanalan needs your help, but I've seen more worthy tumbleweeds roll through the Crossing. You should step out from behind your mummy's frillies and bloody that weapon of yours. Once I find you fit, then I might consider entrusting you with a leve or two."
msgstr "Западному Таналану нужна помощь, а я тут повидал перекати-поле и посолиднее вас. Хватит прятаться за маминой юбкой, пора обагрить клинок! Покажете, на что способны, — может, и доверю вам поручение-другое."

#. ja: やってくれたね。見事なもんじゃないか。<br>さあ、遠慮なく報酬を受け取っておくれ。<br>きっと依頼人も感謝してるだろうさ。
#. de: Den Auftrag hast du gewissenhaft erledigt. Danke dir. Hier ist deine Belohnung.
#. fr: Vous avez accompli la mission sans encombres, à ce que je vois. J'ai bien fait de vous confier ce mandat. Tenez, voilà votre récompense.
#. column 30: Western Thanalan needs your help. Are you <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> enough to give it?
#. column 31: Western Thanalan needs your help, but I've seen more worthy tumbleweeds roll through the Crossing. You should climb your way back to the Adventurers' Guild and make yourself known to the guildmaster. Once I have the approval of the guild, then I might be able to accommodate you with a leve or two.
#. column 32: Good luck and godsspeed!
#. column 33: Western Thanalan needs your help, but I've seen more worthy tumbleweeds roll through the Crossing. You should step out from behind your mummy's frillies and bloody that weapon of yours. Once I find you fit, then I might consider entrusting you with a leve or two.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And with it, the bounty you earned for slaying that wanted target. Impressive work, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. Quite impressive.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:19:0:34"
msgid "I see you are still with us in the realm of Nald. Thal will be disappointed, but He always is. Here is your reward."
msgstr "Вижу, вы всё ещё с нами, в мире Налда. Тал разочарован, но он всегда разочарован. Вот ваша награда."

#. ja: やってくれたね。任務をこなしたうえに、<br>手配していた賞金首まで倒しちまうなんてさ！<br>報酬を増やしておくから、確かめてくれよ。
#. de: Und du hast auch noch Zeit dafür gefunden, das gesuchte Ziel zur Strecke zu bringen! Das Kopfgeld schlage ich auf deine Belohnung drauf.
#. fr: J'ai eu vent de vos exploits. Alors comme ça vous êtes venu<if $gn4>e</if> à bout d'une créature dont la tête était mise à prix<nbsp>? Bravo<nbsp>! Vous pouvez être fi<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if> de vous. J'ai ajouté la prime à la récompense initiale. Tenez...
#. column 30: Western Thanalan needs your help. Are you <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> enough to give it?
#. column 31: Western Thanalan needs your help, but I've seen more worthy tumbleweeds roll through the Crossing. You should climb your way back to the Adventurers' Guild and make yourself known to the guildmaster. Once I have the approval of the guild, then I might be able to accommodate you with a leve or two.
#. column 32: Good luck and godsspeed!
#. column 33: Western Thanalan needs your help, but I've seen more worthy tumbleweeds roll through the Crossing. You should step out from behind your mummy's frillies and bloody that weapon of yours. Once I find you fit, then I might consider entrusting you with a leve or two.
#. column 34: I see you are still with us in the realm of Nald. Thal will be disappointed, but He always is. Here is your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. macro: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split> — the first name of the player character (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <string $gs1> — a text value passed to the string; value = global text 1 (the name of the player character) (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:19:0:37"
msgid "And with it, the bounty you earned for slaying that wanted target. Impressive work, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>. Quite impressive."
msgstr "А вот и награда за голову того, кого вы одолели. Отличная работа, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>. Просто отличная."

#. ja: ここらの住人から冒険者ギルドに寄せられた依頼を、<br>ギルドリーヴとして発行している……。
#. de: Freibriefe! Wir vergeben Freibriefe!<br>Oh hallo! Wenn du danach trachtest, dir einen Namen in dieser Gegend zu machen, sind die Freibriefe eine gute Gelegenheit.
#. fr: Salut <if $gn4>ma grande<else>bonhomme</if>. Si tu cherches à accomplir des mandats de guilde, tu t'es adressé<if $gn4>e</if> à la bonne personne.
#. column 31: Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. The only difference being that they have been approved by <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> of the Adventurers' Guild, and you have not.
#. column 32: See to it then.
#. column 33: Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. The only difference being that they have been approved by me, and you have not. How does one get approval, you ask? Killing, maiming, disemboweling, rending, cleaving, culling. The usual.
#. column 34: The levewatches have reported and I've adjusted your pay accordingly. No complaints, you hear? I get enough from the two mummers flanking me.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Oh, and the bounty. You didn't think I would forget, did you? Did you?
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:20:0:30"
msgid "Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. Good thing we have a lot of it."
msgstr "Работу ищете? Да вы тут не один такой, похоже. Хорошо хоть поручений у нас хватает."

#. ja: ん……仕事を探しているのか……。<br>だが、「ギルドリーヴ」の仕事を受けるには、<br>ギルドの顔役、<switch $n1><case>バデロン<case>ミューヌ<case>モモディ</switch>からの紹介が必要だ。<br>要は相応の実力と信頼が必要だということだ。<br>地道に努力をするんだな……。
#. de: Das Problem ist, dass wir die Freibriefe nur an Abenteurer vergeben dürfen, die die Gilde als zuverlässig erachtet. Sprich doch mal mit <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> um zu erfahren, was du dafür tun musst. Viel Glück!
#. fr: Quoi<nbsp>? Tu cherches du travail<nbsp>? J'aurais bien quelques mandats de guilde à te proposer, malheureusement j'ai pas le droit de donner du boulot aux aventuriers qui ont pas été recommandés par <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>.
#. column 30: Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. Good thing we have a lot of it.
#. column 32: See to it then.
#. column 33: Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. The only difference being that they have been approved by me, and you have not. How does one get approval, you ask? Killing, maiming, disemboweling, rending, cleaving, culling. The usual.
#. column 34: The levewatches have reported and I've adjusted your pay accordingly. No complaints, you hear? I get enough from the two mummers flanking me.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Oh, and the bounty. You didn't think I would forget, did you? Did you?
#. macro: <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:20:0:31"
msgid "Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. The only difference being that they have been approved by <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> of the Adventurers' Guild, and you have not."
msgstr "Работу ищете? Да вы тут не один такой, похоже. Только остальные уже получили одобрение главы Гильдии искателей приключений <switch $n1><case>Бадерона Десятипалого<case>матушки Мионне<case>Момоди Моди</switch>, а вы — нет."

#. ja: そうか、任務に出るのか……<br>成功を祈っているぞ……。
#. de: Alles bereit? Dann viel Erfolg!
#. fr: Bon courage pour ton mandat, et tâche de revenir en un seul morceau.
#. column 30: Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. Good thing we have a lot of it.
#. column 31: Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. The only difference being that they have been approved by <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> of the Adventurers' Guild, and you have not.
#. column 33: Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. The only difference being that they have been approved by me, and you have not. How does one get approval, you ask? Killing, maiming, disemboweling, rending, cleaving, culling. The usual.
#. column 34: The levewatches have reported and I've adjusted your pay accordingly. No complaints, you hear? I get enough from the two mummers flanking me.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Oh, and the bounty. You didn't think I would forget, did you? Did you?
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:20:0:32"
msgid "See to it then."
msgstr "Тогда уж постарайтесь."

#. ja: ん……仕事を探しているのか……。<br>だが、「ギルドリーヴ」の仕事を受けるには、<br>この辺りの魔物に負けぬ「強さ」が必要だ。<br>要は相応の実力と信頼が必要だということだ。<br>地道に努力をするんだな……。
#. de: Das Problem ist, dass wir die Freibriefe nur an erfahrene Abenteurer vergeben dürfen. Wir brauchen Leute, die mit den hiesigen Monstern umgehen können. Warum gehst du nicht raus und sammelst mehr Erfahrung? Viel Glück!
#. fr: Quoi<nbsp>? Tu cherches du travail<nbsp>? Désolé, <if $gn4>ma grande<else>mon grand</if>, mais si tu veux que je te propose des mandats de guilde, il va falloir t'améliorer un peu... Parce que là, même la palefrenière à côté de moi pourrait te botter le cul<nbsp>!
#. column 30: Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. Good thing we have a lot of it.
#. column 31: Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. The only difference being that they have been approved by <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> of the Adventurers' Guild, and you have not.
#. column 32: See to it then.
#. column 34: The levewatches have reported and I've adjusted your pay accordingly. No complaints, you hear? I get enough from the two mummers flanking me.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Oh, and the bounty. You didn't think I would forget, did you? Did you?
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:20:0:33"
msgid "Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. The only difference being that they have been approved by me, and you have not. How does one get approval, you ask? Killing, maiming, disemboweling, rending, cleaving, culling. The usual."
msgstr "Работу ищете? Да вы тут не один такой, похоже. Только у остальных есть моё одобрение, а у вас — нет. Как его получить, спрашиваете? Убивать, калечить, потрошить, рвать на части, рубить, истреблять. Всё как обычно."

#. ja: そうか、任務を達成したか……<br>であれば、報酬を渡さなければならぬな。<br>これが依頼主の感謝の印というわけだ……
#. de: Hast du alles erledigt? Wenn dem so ist, kann ich dir deine Belohnung aushändigen. Dein Auftraggeber ist sicher sehr dankbar.
#. fr: On dirait que t'as réussi le mandat que je t'ai confié. Tout travail mérite salaire. Voilà donc ta récompense.
#. column 30: Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. Good thing we have a lot of it.
#. column 31: Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. The only difference being that they have been approved by <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> of the Adventurers' Guild, and you have not.
#. column 32: See to it then.
#. column 33: Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. The only difference being that they have been approved by me, and you have not. How does one get approval, you ask? Killing, maiming, disemboweling, rending, cleaving, culling. The usual.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: Oh, and the bounty. You didn't think I would forget, did you? Did you?
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:20:0:34"
msgid "The levewatches have reported and I've adjusted your pay accordingly. No complaints, you hear? I get enough from the two mummers flanking me."
msgstr "Смотрители доложили о ваших успехах, и я назначил плату соответственно. Без жалоб, ясно? Мне и от двух шутов по бокам хватает."

#. ja: ほう、任務を達成したうえ、賞金首も倒したのか……<br>となれば報酬を上乗せせざるを得まい。<br>よくやってくれたな……。
#. de: Das Kopfgeld für das gesuchte Ziel habe ich schon dazugerechnet. Saubere Arbeit, muss ich sagen.
#. fr: Quoi<nbsp>? T'as tué une créature recherchée, tu dis<nbsp>!? C'est fantastique<nbsp>! Les habitants de la métairie seront ravis d'apprendre la nouvelle. Tiens, j'ai ajouté un petit bonus à ta récompense, en guise de re<shy>mer<shy>cie<shy>ment.
#. column 30: Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. Good thing we have a lot of it.
#. column 31: Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. The only difference being that they have been approved by <switch $n1><case>Baderon Tenfingers<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> of the Adventurers' Guild, and you have not.
#. column 32: See to it then.
#. column 33: Here for work, are you? You and everyone else, it seems. The only difference being that they have been approved by me, and you have not. How does one get approval, you ask? Killing, maiming, disemboweling, rending, cleaving, culling. The usual.
#. column 34: The levewatches have reported and I've adjusted your pay accordingly. No complaints, you hear? I get enough from the two mummers flanking me.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:20:0:37"
msgid "Oh, and the bounty. You didn't think I would forget, did you? Did you?"
msgstr "А, и награда за голову. Не думали же вы, что я о ней забуду? Не думали?"

#. ja: コスタ・デル・ソル近辺の案件を、<br>ギルドリーヴとして発行しているぜ。<br>やる気と腕がある冒険者なら、大歓迎だ。
#. de: Ich vergebe Freibriefe für die Sonnenküste. Aber glaub nicht, dass du dich an der schönen Küste ausruhen kannst. Die meisten Aufträge sind lebens<shy>ge<shy>fähr<shy>lich.
#. fr: <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>Bonsoir<else>Bonjour</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>Bonjour<else>Bonsoir</if></if> aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>. Est-ce que vous êtes en quête de travail<nbsp>? Si c'est le cas, il se peut que j'aie de quoi vous occuper.
#. column 31: Used to be a 'Cuda. Manned the camp right beyond Limsa... Manned it that is, till I lost my big toe. A chunk of Dalamud fell straight on it. Consider myself lucky, though. Another ilm to the left, I'd have lost a lot more than that. Now, as for you... I've no leves for you. <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>'s orders. Haul your arse back to the Adventurers' Guild if you've a problem with that.
#. column 32: Till sea swallows <i>you</i>! Gah hah hah!
#. column 33: Used to be a 'Cuda. Manned the camp right beyond Limsa... Manned it that is, till I lost my big toe. A chunk of Dalamud fell straight on it. Consider myself lucky, though. Another ilm to the left, I'd have lost a lot more than that. Now, as for you... I've no leves for you. <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> made it clear I'm to issue no quests to those without at least a few scars to prove their worth.
#. column 34: Look who's returned all giddy as a gil turtle. Now take the coin and be off with you.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And one last thing before you go─your share of the bounty. Unless you think I should keep it? Gah hah hah!
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:21:0:30"
msgid "Another adventurer, eh? A man can move to the very edge of the realm and he'll still bump into one of your kind. I suppose it's not all bad, though. Especially when there are leves to be done."
msgstr "Ещё один искатель приключений, значит? Хоть на край света переберись — всё равно на таких, как вы, наткнёшься. Хотя, может, это и неплохо. Особенно когда поручений полно."

#. ja: 「ギルドリーヴ」の仕事をしたいってのかい？<br>参ったな、この仕事は相応の実力者にしか<br>任せられないんだよ。<br>まずは冒険者ギルドの顔役、<br><switch $n1><case>バデロンの旦那<case>ミューヌの姉ちゃん<case>モモディさん</switch>からの紹介を<br>受けてきてくれるかな？
#. de: Du willst dich also an einem Freibrief versuchen? Hm, so einfach ist das nicht. Ich darf die Aufträge nur an Abenteurer vergeben, für deren Können die Aben<shy>teurer<shy>gilde ausdrücklich bürgt. Kehre zur Gilde zurück und sprich mit <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>.
#. fr: Je suis chargé de gérer les mandats de guilde à Costa del Sol. J'imagine que vous savez de quoi il s'agit, je ne vais donc pas entrer dans les détails. Sachez toutefois que je ne peux pas donner de travail aux aventuriers qui n'ont pas obtenu de re<shy>com<shy>man<shy>da<shy>tion de la part de <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>. Eh oui, c'est comme ça...
#. column 30: Another adventurer, eh? A man can move to the very edge of the realm and he'll still bump into one of your kind. I suppose it's not all bad, though. Especially when there are leves to be done.
#. column 32: Till sea swallows <i>you</i>! Gah hah hah!
#. column 33: Used to be a 'Cuda. Manned the camp right beyond Limsa... Manned it that is, till I lost my big toe. A chunk of Dalamud fell straight on it. Consider myself lucky, though. Another ilm to the left, I'd have lost a lot more than that. Now, as for you... I've no leves for you. <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> made it clear I'm to issue no quests to those without at least a few scars to prove their worth.
#. column 34: Look who's returned all giddy as a gil turtle. Now take the coin and be off with you.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And one last thing before you go─your share of the bounty. Unless you think I should keep it? Gah hah hah!
#. macro: <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:21:0:31"
msgid "Used to be a 'Cuda. Manned the camp right beyond Limsa... Manned it that is, till I lost my big toe. A chunk of Dalamud fell straight on it. Consider myself lucky, though. Another ilm to the left, I'd have lost a lot more than that. Now, as for you... I've no leves for you. <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>'s orders. Haul your arse back to the Adventurers' Guild if you've a problem with that."
msgstr "Раньше я служил в «Кудах». Стоял в лагере за Лимсой... то есть стоял, пока мне большой палец не оторвало. Кусок Даламида угодил прямо в него. Ещё бы на лад левее — и потерял бы куда больше. А вам поручений не видать. Так приказал <switch $n1> <case>Бадерон<case>матушка Мионне<case>Момоди Моди</switch>. Что-то не нравится — тащите свою задницу обратно в Гильдию искателей приключений."

#. ja: よし、それじゃあ、一働きしてきてくれ。<br>しっかり頼んだぜ！
#. de: Auf geht's! Der Freibrief erledigt sich nicht von alleine!
#. fr: Bon courage<nbsp>! Je compte sur vous<nbsp>!
#. column 30: Another adventurer, eh? A man can move to the very edge of the realm and he'll still bump into one of your kind. I suppose it's not all bad, though. Especially when there are leves to be done.
#. column 31: Used to be a 'Cuda. Manned the camp right beyond Limsa... Manned it that is, till I lost my big toe. A chunk of Dalamud fell straight on it. Consider myself lucky, though. Another ilm to the left, I'd have lost a lot more than that. Now, as for you... I've no leves for you. <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>'s orders. Haul your arse back to the Adventurers' Guild if you've a problem with that.
#. column 33: Used to be a 'Cuda. Manned the camp right beyond Limsa... Manned it that is, till I lost my big toe. A chunk of Dalamud fell straight on it. Consider myself lucky, though. Another ilm to the left, I'd have lost a lot more than that. Now, as for you... I've no leves for you. <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> made it clear I'm to issue no quests to those without at least a few scars to prove their worth.
#. column 34: Look who's returned all giddy as a gil turtle. Now take the coin and be off with you.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And one last thing before you go─your share of the bounty. Unless you think I should keep it? Gah hah hah!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:21:0:32"
msgid "Till sea swallows <i>you</i>! Gah hah hah!"
msgstr "Пусть море проглотит <i>вас</i>! Га-ха-ха!"

#. ja: 「ギルドリーヴ」の仕事をしたいってのかい？<br>参ったな、この仕事は相応の実力者にしか<br>任せられないんだよ。<br>この辺りにいる魔物を、<br>ちょちょいと片付けられるくらいの<br>実力をつけてから、また来てくれ。
#. de: Du willst dich also an einem Freibrief versuchen? Hm, so einfach ist das nicht. Ich darf die Aufträge nur an Abenteurer vergeben, die ihr Können im Kampf bewiesen haben. Warum gehst du nicht raus und erledigst ein paar Monster, um deine Durchsetzungskraft im Kampf zu stärken?
#. fr: Je suis chargé gérer les mandats de guilde à Costa del Sol. J'imagine que vous savez de quoi il s'agit, je ne vais donc pas entrer dans les détails. Sachez toutefois que je ne peux pas donner de travail aux aventuriers qui ne sont pas suf<shy>fi<shy>sam<shy>ment puissants pour tuer les monstres qui rôdent autour du camp. Eh oui, c'est comme ça...
#. column 30: Another adventurer, eh? A man can move to the very edge of the realm and he'll still bump into one of your kind. I suppose it's not all bad, though. Especially when there are leves to be done.
#. column 31: Used to be a 'Cuda. Manned the camp right beyond Limsa... Manned it that is, till I lost my big toe. A chunk of Dalamud fell straight on it. Consider myself lucky, though. Another ilm to the left, I'd have lost a lot more than that. Now, as for you... I've no leves for you. <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>'s orders. Haul your arse back to the Adventurers' Guild if you've a problem with that.
#. column 32: Till sea swallows <i>you</i>! Gah hah hah!
#. column 34: Look who's returned all giddy as a gil turtle. Now take the coin and be off with you.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And one last thing before you go─your share of the bounty. Unless you think I should keep it? Gah hah hah!
#. macro: <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:21:0:33"
msgid "Used to be a 'Cuda. Manned the camp right beyond Limsa... Manned it that is, till I lost my big toe. A chunk of Dalamud fell straight on it. Consider myself lucky, though. Another ilm to the left, I'd have lost a lot more than that. Now, as for you... I've no leves for you. <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> made it clear I'm to issue no quests to those without at least a few scars to prove their worth."
msgstr "Раньше я служил в «Кудах». Стоял в лагере за Лимсой... то есть стоял, пока мне большой палец не оторвало. Кусок Даламида угодил прямо в него. Ещё бы на лад левее — и потерял бы куда больше. А вам поручений не видать. <switch $n1><case>Бадерон<case>матушка Мионне<case>Момоди Моди</switch> ясно дал понять: поручений не давать тем, у кого нет хотя бы пары шрамов, подтверждающих их заслуги."

#. ja: おっと、もう一仕事終えたってのかい？<br>ありがとよ、大助かりってもんだぜ。<br>さ、報酬を受け取ってくれ！
#. de: Du bist schon fertig? Alles erledigt? Alle Achtung, den Freibrief hast du sauber erledigt. Hier ist deine Belohnung.
#. fr: Vous avez accompli le mandat<nbsp>? Splendide<nbsp>! Je savais bien que vous en étiez capable. Tenez, voici la récompense qui vous est due.
#. column 30: Another adventurer, eh? A man can move to the very edge of the realm and he'll still bump into one of your kind. I suppose it's not all bad, though. Especially when there are leves to be done.
#. column 31: Used to be a 'Cuda. Manned the camp right beyond Limsa... Manned it that is, till I lost my big toe. A chunk of Dalamud fell straight on it. Consider myself lucky, though. Another ilm to the left, I'd have lost a lot more than that. Now, as for you... I've no leves for you. <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>'s orders. Haul your arse back to the Adventurers' Guild if you've a problem with that.
#. column 32: Till sea swallows <i>you</i>! Gah hah hah!
#. column 33: Used to be a 'Cuda. Manned the camp right beyond Limsa... Manned it that is, till I lost my big toe. A chunk of Dalamud fell straight on it. Consider myself lucky, though. Another ilm to the left, I'd have lost a lot more than that. Now, as for you... I've no leves for you. <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> made it clear I'm to issue no quests to those without at least a few scars to prove their worth.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And one last thing before you go─your share of the bounty. Unless you think I should keep it? Gah hah hah!
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:21:0:34"
msgid "Look who's returned all giddy as a gil turtle. Now take the coin and be off with you."
msgstr "Гляньте-ка, кто вернулся — прямо сияет, как гиловая черепаха! Забирайте монеты и ступайте."

#. ja: 一仕事終えたうえに、賞金首も倒しただって？<br>こいつは、たまげた……大助かりってもんだぜ。<br>さ、割り増しした報酬を受け取ってくれ！
#. de: Das gesuchte Ziel hast du auch zur Strecke gebracht. Dann lass mich das Kopfgeld auf deine Belohnung aufschlagen. Gute Arbeit!
#. fr: Vous êtes venu<if $gn4>e</if> à bout d'une créature recherchée, vous dites<nbsp>!? Alors ça, pour une nouvelle, c'est une excellente nouvelle<nbsp>! Le seigneur Gegeruju sera ravi d'entendre ça. Tenez, voici votre récompense et la prime de tête qui va avec.
#. column 30: Another adventurer, eh? A man can move to the very edge of the realm and he'll still bump into one of your kind. I suppose it's not all bad, though. Especially when there are leves to be done.
#. column 31: Used to be a 'Cuda. Manned the camp right beyond Limsa... Manned it that is, till I lost my big toe. A chunk of Dalamud fell straight on it. Consider myself lucky, though. Another ilm to the left, I'd have lost a lot more than that. Now, as for you... I've no leves for you. <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>'s orders. Haul your arse back to the Adventurers' Guild if you've a problem with that.
#. column 32: Till sea swallows <i>you</i>! Gah hah hah!
#. column 33: Used to be a 'Cuda. Manned the camp right beyond Limsa... Manned it that is, till I lost my big toe. A chunk of Dalamud fell straight on it. Consider myself lucky, though. Another ilm to the left, I'd have lost a lot more than that. Now, as for you... I've no leves for you. <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> made it clear I'm to issue no quests to those without at least a few scars to prove their worth.
#. column 34: Look who's returned all giddy as a gil turtle. Now take the coin and be off with you.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:21:0:37"
msgid "And one last thing before you go─your share of the bounty. Unless you think I should keep it? Gah hah hah!"
msgstr "И напоследок — ваша доля награды за голову. Или думаете, мне её оставить? Га-ха-ха!"

#. ja: 「モラビー造船廠」近辺の任務を、<br>ギルドリーヴとして発行しておる。
#. de: Ich biete Freibriefe für die Region um das Trockendock an. Hier lässt sich schnell ein hübsches Sümmchen verdienen, wenn du fleißig bist.
#. fr: Mon petit doigt me dit que tu cherches quelque chose pour t'occuper. Figure-toi que je suis justement ici pour donner du travail aux aventuriers désœuvrés, comme toi.
#. column 31: The Adventurers' Guild has strict rules on who can and cannot partake in levequests. You fall in the latter half, as you have not received specific permission from guildmaster <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>.
#. column 32: May the Navigator guide you!
#. column 33: The Adventurers' Guild has strict rules on who can and cannot partake in levequests. You fall in the latter half, as you have yet to prove yourself capable of handling the type of tasks I offer. Hone your skills in battle, and I may reconsider.
#. column 34: You were quick to return. The levemetes have only just reported your accomplishments. Allow me a moment to prepare your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And here is the bounty for the wanted target. It would be a shame if your efforts went unrecognized.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:22:0:30"
msgid "Well met. Let us find a leve that suits your talents."
msgstr "Рад встрече. Подберём поручение вам по силам."

#. ja: 「ギルドリーヴ」の仕事を探しているのか？<br>だとすれば、お前には先に成すべきことがある。<br><key>冒険者ギルドの顔役、<switch $n1><case>バデロン<case>ミューヌ<case>モモディ</switch>から、<br>紹介を受ける、という大切な手順がな……。<br>実力者にしか、任務は任せられんのだ。
#. de: Gut. Dann muss ich nur noch deine Empfehlung durch die Aben<shy>teurer<shy>gilde überprüfen ... Hm, sieht so aus, als wärst du noch nicht empfohlen worden. Sprich mit <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>, um die Sache zu regeln. Dann kann ich dir Arbeit anbieten.
#. fr: Mon nom est Ourawann. Je suis chargé d'attribuer des mandats de guilde pour le chantier naval de Moraby. Tu sais sans doute de quoi il s'agit, et je ne vais donc pas me lancer dans de longues ex<shy>pli<shy>ca<shy>tions. Sache toutefois que je ne peux pas donner de travail aux aventuriers qui n'ont pas obtenu de re<shy>com<shy>man<shy>da<shy>tion de la part de <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>. Me regarde pas comme ça, c'est pas moi qui décide des règles<nbsp>!
#. column 30: Well met. Let us find a leve that suits your talents.
#. column 32: May the Navigator guide you!
#. column 33: The Adventurers' Guild has strict rules on who can and cannot partake in levequests. You fall in the latter half, as you have yet to prove yourself capable of handling the type of tasks I offer. Hone your skills in battle, and I may reconsider.
#. column 34: You were quick to return. The levemetes have only just reported your accomplishments. Allow me a moment to prepare your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And here is the bounty for the wanted target. It would be a shame if your efforts went unrecognized.
#. macro: <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:22:0:31"
msgid "The Adventurers' Guild has strict rules on who can and cannot partake in levequests. You fall in the latter half, as you have not received specific permission from guildmaster <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>."
msgstr "У Гильдии искателей приключений строгие правила: кому можно выполнять гильдейские поручения, а кому нельзя. Вам нельзя — глава Гильдии <switch $n1><case>Бадерон<case>матушка Мионне<case>Момоди Моди</switch> ещё не дал вам особого разрешения."

#. ja: いいか、無闇に突っ込むんじゃないぞ。<br>冷静に、確実に任務を達成するんだ。
#. de: Viel Erfolg bei deinem Auftrag. Pass gut auf dich auf!
#. fr: Prépare-toi bien avant de lancer le mandat. C'est que je ne veux pas non plus t'envoyer au casse-pipe.
#. column 30: Well met. Let us find a leve that suits your talents.
#. column 31: The Adventurers' Guild has strict rules on who can and cannot partake in levequests. You fall in the latter half, as you have not received specific permission from guildmaster <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>.
#. column 33: The Adventurers' Guild has strict rules on who can and cannot partake in levequests. You fall in the latter half, as you have yet to prove yourself capable of handling the type of tasks I offer. Hone your skills in battle, and I may reconsider.
#. column 34: You were quick to return. The levemetes have only just reported your accomplishments. Allow me a moment to prepare your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And here is the bounty for the wanted target. It would be a shame if your efforts went unrecognized.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:22:0:32"
msgid "May the Navigator guide you!"
msgstr "Да сопутствует вам мореплаватель!"

#. ja: 「ギルドリーヴ」の仕事を探しているのか？<br>だとすれば、お前には先に成すべきことがある。<br><key>この辺りの凶暴な魔物を、一ひねりにできるだけの<br>腕を身に着ける、という大切な手順がな……。<br>実力者にしか、任務は任せられんのだ。
#. de: Hm, sieht so aus, als fehlte es dir noch an Erfahrung. Komm doch später noch einmal wieder, nachdem du mehr Monster aus dieser Region gejagt hast.
#. fr: Mon nom est Ourawann. Je suis chargé d'attribuer des mandats de guilde pour le chantier naval de Moraby. Tu sais sans doute de quoi il s'agit, et je ne vais donc pas me lancer dans de longues ex<shy>pli<shy>ca<shy>tions. Sache toutefois que je ne peux pas donner de travail aux aventuriers qui ne sont pas suf<shy>fi<shy>sam<shy>ment aguerris pour tuer les monstres qui rôdent autour du chantier naval. Me regarde pas comme ça, c'est pas moi qui décide des règles<nbsp>!
#. column 30: Well met. Let us find a leve that suits your talents.
#. column 31: The Adventurers' Guild has strict rules on who can and cannot partake in levequests. You fall in the latter half, as you have not received specific permission from guildmaster <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>.
#. column 32: May the Navigator guide you!
#. column 34: You were quick to return. The levemetes have only just reported your accomplishments. Allow me a moment to prepare your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And here is the bounty for the wanted target. It would be a shame if your efforts went unrecognized.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:22:0:33"
msgid "The Adventurers' Guild has strict rules on who can and cannot partake in levequests. You fall in the latter half, as you have yet to prove yourself capable of handling the type of tasks I offer. Hone your skills in battle, and I may reconsider."
msgstr "У Гильдии искателей приключений строгие правила: кому можно выполнять гильдейские поручения, а кому нельзя. Вам пока нельзя — вы ещё не доказали, что справитесь с моими заданиями. Потренируйтесь в бою, и я, пожалуй, передумаю."

#. ja: その様子だと、任務は達成できたようだな。<br>ご苦労……きっと依頼主も感謝しているだろう。<br>さあ、報酬を受け取るのだ。
#. de: Willkommen zurück! Ich gratuliere dir zu deinem Erfolg. Dein Auftraggeber ist sehr zufrieden und möchte, dass ich dir diese Belohnung aushändige.
#. fr: Tu as accompli le mandat que je t'avais confié<nbsp>? Très bien. Voici la récompense qui va avec.
#. column 30: Well met. Let us find a leve that suits your talents.
#. column 31: The Adventurers' Guild has strict rules on who can and cannot partake in levequests. You fall in the latter half, as you have not received specific permission from guildmaster <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>.
#. column 32: May the Navigator guide you!
#. column 33: The Adventurers' Guild has strict rules on who can and cannot partake in levequests. You fall in the latter half, as you have yet to prove yourself capable of handling the type of tasks I offer. Hone your skills in battle, and I may reconsider.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: And here is the bounty for the wanted target. It would be a shame if your efforts went unrecognized.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:22:0:34"
msgid "You were quick to return. The levemetes have only just reported your accomplishments. Allow me a moment to prepare your reward."
msgstr "Вы быстро вернулись. Смотрители поручений только что доложили о ваших успехах. Подождите немного, я приготовлю награду."

#. ja: なるほど、任務中に賞金首も討伐したのか。<br>よし、それでは報酬も上乗せしておこう。
#. de: Außerdem gebe ich dir noch das Kopfgeld für das gesuchte Ziel, das du erledigt hast. Auf dich ist wirklich Verlass!
#. fr: Non seulement tu as réussi le mandat que je t'ai confié, mais en plus tu es venu<if $gn4>e</if> à bout d'une créature recherchée... Chapeau<nbsp>! On peut dif<shy>fi<shy>ci<shy>le<shy>ment faire mieux, je crois. Voilà ta récompense, et la prime de tête qui va avec. Fais-en bon usage<nbsp>!
#. column 30: Well met. Let us find a leve that suits your talents.
#. column 31: The Adventurers' Guild has strict rules on who can and cannot partake in levequests. You fall in the latter half, as you have not received specific permission from guildmaster <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>.
#. column 32: May the Navigator guide you!
#. column 33: The Adventurers' Guild has strict rules on who can and cannot partake in levequests. You fall in the latter half, as you have yet to prove yourself capable of handling the type of tasks I offer. Hone your skills in battle, and I may reconsider.
#. column 34: You were quick to return. The levemetes have only just reported your accomplishments. Allow me a moment to prepare your reward.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:22:0:37"
msgid "And here is the bounty for the wanted target. It would be a shame if your efforts went unrecognized."
msgstr "Вот и награда за голову разыскиваемой цели. Было бы обидно, если бы ваши старания остались без награды."

#. ja: アタシは、ク・レータイ。<br>冒険者ギルドから、この近辺を任地とする<br>「ギルドリーヴ」発行を任されている者だよ。
#. de: Ich bin K'leytai und habe gerade ein paar alte Freibriefe ausgegraben. Schau sie dir an.
#. fr: Salut à toi, aventurrri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>. J'ai été envoyée ici pour distribuer les mandats de guilde.
#. column 31: Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. Your body may have weathered the journey here, and you may have the skill to overcome the hardships of this forsaken land. But, whether you can be trusted to fulfill the tasks I offer is not for me to decide. I leave that to guildmaster <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>.
#. column 32: Mor Dhona is an unforgiving place, and may prove an even more formidable foe than the leve objectives themselves. You would do well not to forget this.
#. column 33: Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. I know not how one of such little experience may have found me, but I cannot allow you any of my leves, simply because I fear you incapable of completing any of them alive.
#. column 34: Ask any adventurer and they will tell you, a successful Mor Dhonan levequest is one you come back from alive.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: To slay a wanted target in addition to returning alive is nothing short of a miracle. If anyone deserved this bounty, it is you.
#. macro: <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:23:0:30"
msgid "Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. You don't appear soft, but appearances aren't everything. We shall let Mor Dhona decide if you are truly worthy."
msgstr "Мордона — суровый край, и чтобы пережить опасности, таящиеся в его гибельной красоте, нужно быть ещё суровее. Вы не кажетесь слабым человеком, но внешность бывает обманчива. Пусть сама Мордона решит, достойны ли вы."

#. ja: おや、働き口でも探してるのかい？<br>それなら、いい相手に話しかけたもんだね。<br>なにせアタシは「ギルドリーヴ」の発行人なのさ。<br>だけど、今のアンタには発行できないよ。<br><switch $n1><case>バデロン<case>ミューヌ<case>モモディ</switch>さんからの紹介がない人には<br>「ギルドリーヴ」は任せられないのさ。
#. de: Ich bin leider nicht berechtigt, die Autorität von <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch> zu untergraben. Du musst zuerst mit <switch $n1><case>ihm<case>ihr<case>ihr</switch> sprechen, wenn du einen Freibrief von mir willst.
#. fr: Tiens, tu ne chercherais pas du trrravail, par hasard<nbsp>? Je pourrais t'en confier, mais tu vas d'abord devoir obtenir la re<shy>com<shy>man<shy>da<shy>tion de <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Miounne<case>Momodi</switch>. La guilde des aventuriers ne peut pas faire confiance <if $gn4>à la première venue<else>au premier venu</if>, tu comprends<nbsp>?
#. column 30: Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. You don't appear soft, but appearances aren't everything. We shall let Mor Dhona decide if you are truly worthy.
#. column 32: Mor Dhona is an unforgiving place, and may prove an even more formidable foe than the leve objectives themselves. You would do well not to forget this.
#. column 33: Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. I know not how one of such little experience may have found me, but I cannot allow you any of my leves, simply because I fear you incapable of completing any of them alive.
#. column 34: Ask any adventurer and they will tell you, a successful Mor Dhonan levequest is one you come back from alive.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: To slay a wanted target in addition to returning alive is nothing short of a miracle. If anyone deserved this bounty, it is you.
#. macro: <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch> — shows the case whose position equals the value: the first <case> for 1, the second for 2, …; value = number parameter 1 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:23:0:31"
msgid "Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. Your body may have weathered the journey here, and you may have the skill to overcome the hardships of this forsaken land. But, whether you can be trusted to fulfill the tasks I offer is not for me to decide. I leave that to guildmaster <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>."
msgstr "Мордона — суровый край, и чтобы пережить опасности, таящиеся в его гибельной красоте, нужно быть ещё суровее. Вы, может, и добрались сюда, и, возможно, сумеете одолеть все тяготы этой забытой богами земли. Но могу ли я доверить вам свои поручения — решать не мне. Это решит глава Гильдии искателей приключений <switch $n1><case>Бадерон<case>матушка Мионне<case>Момоди Моди</switch>."

#. ja: がんばってね。<br>アンタの無事を祈っているからさ。
#. de: Streng dich an, oder du kannst die Hoffnung auf eine Belohnung begraben!
#. fr: Bon courrrage<nbsp>! Je vais prier pour ton retour en un seul morceau, héhé.
#. column 30: Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. You don't appear soft, but appearances aren't everything. We shall let Mor Dhona decide if you are truly worthy.
#. column 31: Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. Your body may have weathered the journey here, and you may have the skill to overcome the hardships of this forsaken land. But, whether you can be trusted to fulfill the tasks I offer is not for me to decide. I leave that to guildmaster <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>.
#. column 33: Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. I know not how one of such little experience may have found me, but I cannot allow you any of my leves, simply because I fear you incapable of completing any of them alive.
#. column 34: Ask any adventurer and they will tell you, a successful Mor Dhonan levequest is one you come back from alive.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: To slay a wanted target in addition to returning alive is nothing short of a miracle. If anyone deserved this bounty, it is you.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:23:0:32"
msgid "Mor Dhona is an unforgiving place, and may prove an even more formidable foe than the leve objectives themselves. You would do well not to forget this."
msgstr "Мордона не прощает ошибок и порой опаснее, чем само поручение. Не забывайте об этом."

#. ja: おや、働き口でも探してるのかい？<br>それなら、いい相手に話しかけたもんだね。<br>なにせアタシは「ギルドリーヴ」の発行人なのさ。<br>だけど、今のアンタには発行できないよ。<br>この辺りの魔物に負けない実力をつけたら、<br>また声をかけてちょうだい。
#. de: Tut mir leid, dir das Wasser abgraben zu müssen, aber du bist leider noch nicht erfahren genug für diese Freibriefe. Verbessere dich noch ein wenig, indem du ein paar Monster aus dieser Gegend erlegst.
#. fr: Tiens, tu ne chercherais pas du trrravail, par hasard<nbsp>? Je pourrais t'en confier, mais tu vas d'abord devoir t'entraîner davantage. La guilde des aventuriers ne peut pas faire confiance <if $gn4>à la première venue<else>au premier venu</if>, tu comprends<nbsp>?
#. column 30: Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. You don't appear soft, but appearances aren't everything. We shall let Mor Dhona decide if you are truly worthy.
#. column 31: Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. Your body may have weathered the journey here, and you may have the skill to overcome the hardships of this forsaken land. But, whether you can be trusted to fulfill the tasks I offer is not for me to decide. I leave that to guildmaster <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>.
#. column 32: Mor Dhona is an unforgiving place, and may prove an even more formidable foe than the leve objectives themselves. You would do well not to forget this.
#. column 34: Ask any adventurer and they will tell you, a successful Mor Dhonan levequest is one you come back from alive.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: To slay a wanted target in addition to returning alive is nothing short of a miracle. If anyone deserved this bounty, it is you.
#. macro: <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:23:0:33"
msgid "Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. I know not how one of such little experience may have found me, but I cannot allow you any of my leves, simply because I fear you incapable of completing any of them alive."
msgstr "Мордона — суровый край, и чтобы пережить опасности, таящиеся в его гибельной красоте, нужно быть ещё суровее. Не знаю, как вас сюда занесло, но поручений я вам не дам: боюсь, живыми вы с них не вернётесь."

#. ja: おかえりなさい。<br>アンタの働きには、きっと依頼人も満足するはずさ。<br>それじゃ、お待ちかねの報酬を渡そうじゃないか。
#. de: Gut gemacht! Deine Belohnung hatte ich aus Angst vor Übergriffen bis zu deiner Rückkehr dort drüben im Boden vergraben ... Hier, nimm!
#. fr: Ah, je suis heurrreuse de te revoir<nbsp>! Notre client sera cer<shy>tai<shy>ne<shy>ment ravi de ta performance. Tiens, voilà ta paye.
#. column 30: Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. You don't appear soft, but appearances aren't everything. We shall let Mor Dhona decide if you are truly worthy.
#. column 31: Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. Your body may have weathered the journey here, and you may have the skill to overcome the hardships of this forsaken land. But, whether you can be trusted to fulfill the tasks I offer is not for me to decide. I leave that to guildmaster <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>.
#. column 32: Mor Dhona is an unforgiving place, and may prove an even more formidable foe than the leve objectives themselves. You would do well not to forget this.
#. column 33: Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. I know not how one of such little experience may have found me, but I cannot allow you any of my leves, simply because I fear you incapable of completing any of them alive.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: To slay a wanted target in addition to returning alive is nothing short of a miracle. If anyone deserved this bounty, it is you.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:23:0:34"
msgid "Ask any adventurer and they will tell you, a successful Mor Dhonan levequest is one you come back from alive."
msgstr "Спроси любого искателя приключений: успешное поручение в Мордоне — то, после которого возвращаются живыми."

#. ja: それから、任務に加えて、賞金首も倒したんだって？<br>報酬を上乗せしない訳にはいかないね。
#. de: Ha! Deine zukünftigen Gegner werden sich auf der Stelle eingraben lassen, wenn sie erfahren, wie du dir dieses Kopfgeld verdient hast!
#. fr: Incroyable<nbsp>! Tu as même réussi à abattre une créature recherchée<nbsp>! Dans ce cas, tu as bien mérité cette récompense sup<shy>plé<shy>men<shy>tai<shy>re. Brrravo<nbsp>!
#. column 30: Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. You don't appear soft, but appearances aren't everything. We shall let Mor Dhona decide if you are truly worthy.
#. column 31: Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. Your body may have weathered the journey here, and you may have the skill to overcome the hardships of this forsaken land. But, whether you can be trusted to fulfill the tasks I offer is not for me to decide. I leave that to guildmaster <switch $n1><case>Baderon<case>Mother Miounne<case>Momodi Modi</switch>.
#. column 32: Mor Dhona is an unforgiving place, and may prove an even more formidable foe than the leve objectives themselves. You would do well not to forget this.
#. column 33: Mor Dhona is a hard place, and it takes an even harder <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> to survive the challenges that lurk amidst its deadly beauty. I know not how one of such little experience may have found me, but I cannot allow you any of my leves, simply because I fear you incapable of completing any of them alive.
#. column 34: Ask any adventurer and they will tell you, a successful Mor Dhonan levequest is one you come back from alive.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:23:0:37"
msgid "To slay a wanted target in addition to returning alive is nothing short of a miracle. If anyone deserved this bounty, it is you."
msgstr "Одолеть разыскиваемую цель и при этом вернуться живым — настоящее чудо. Если кто и заслужил эту награду, так это вы."

#. ja: 自分は、黒渦団に所属するユージーン甲曹長。<br>「グランドカンパニーリーヴ」の発行を担当している。
#. de: Ahoi! Ich bin Sturmmaat 1. Klasse Eugene, stets dem Mahlstrom zu Diensten. Nur keine Müdigkeit vorschützen, versuch dich an einem Staatserlass!
#. fr: Mon nom est Eugene. Je suis chargé d'attribuer des mandats de grande compagnie pour le Maelstrom.
#. column 31: I am not authorized to issue quests to those who have yet to prove themselves to the realm. Perhaps you should try your hand at several guildleves from the local Adventurers' Guild.
#. column 32: May the Navigator guide you, <if ($gn52 > 0)><sheet GCRankLimsaMaleText $gn52 0></if><if ($gn53 > 0)><sheet GCRankGridaniaMaleText $gn53 0></if><if ($gn54 > 0)><sheet GCRankUldahMaleText $gn54 0></if> <split " " 2><string $gs1></split>!
#. column 33: I am not authorized to issue quests to those who have yet to prove themselves to the realm. Perhaps you should try your hand at several guildleves from the local Adventurers' Guild.
#. column 34: Your contribution has been noted, <if ($gn52 > 0)><sheet GCRankLimsaMaleText $gn52 0></if><if ($gn53 > 0)><sheet GCRankGridaniaMaleText $gn53 0></if><if ($gn54 > 0)><sheet GCRankUldahMaleText $gn54 0></if> <split " " 2><string $gs1></split>, and your seals prepared.
#. column 35: Someone high up believed that it would be a fine idea to allow members from any Grand Company to accept leves meant for the Maelstrom. I personally do not agree, but I have my orders. They did <i>not</i> mention aught of allowing those adventurers who had yet to pledge their allegiance to even the lowly Order of the Twin Adder, let alone the mighty Maelstrom.
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:24:0:30"
msgid "I am Storm Sergeant First Class Eugene Rivers, charged with the issuing of Grand Company levequests."
msgstr "Я старший сержант первого класса Эжен Риверс из Водоворота. Отвечаю за выдачу поручений Великих компаний."

#. ja: 「ギルドリーヴ」の経験がある者がいれば、<br>この任務を任せることができるのだが……。<br>軍令部に、兵を回すように上申せねば！
#. de: Mit Grünschnäbeln kann ich nichts anfangen, aber wer schon mal einen Gilden<shy>frei<shy>brief absolviert hat, kann sich jederzeit bei mir zum Dienst melden.
#. fr: Vous voulez que je vous propose des mandats de grande compagnie<nbsp>? Je suis désolé, mais je ne suis pas autorisé à confier des missions aux aventuriers qui n'ont pas encore accompli un seul mandat de guilde.
#. column 30: I am Storm Sergeant First Class Eugene Rivers, charged with the issuing of Grand Company levequests.
#. column 32: May the Navigator guide you, <if ($gn52 > 0)><sheet GCRankLimsaMaleText $gn52 0></if><if ($gn53 > 0)><sheet GCRankGridaniaMaleText $gn53 0></if><if ($gn54 > 0)><sheet GCRankUldahMaleText $gn54 0></if> <split " " 2><string $gs1></split>!
