msgid "I've no time for those who've yet to butt horns with a hapalit."
msgstr "Мне некогда возиться с теми, кому ещё не доводилось скрестить рога с хапалитом."

#. ja: <string $gs1><if ($gn52 > 0)><sheet GCRankLimsaMaleText $gn52 0></if><if ($gn53 > 0)><sheet GCRankGridaniaMaleText $gn53 0></if><if ($gn54 > 0)><sheet GCRankUldahMaleText $gn54 0></if>の帰還を確認！<br>規定に従い、軍票を支給するのであります！<br>お疲れ様でありましたぁ！！
#. de: Du bist hart im Nehmen und deshalb sehr erfolgreich, <if ($gn52 > 0)><if $gn4><sheet GCRankLimsaFemaleText $gn52 0><else><sheet GCRankLimsaMaleText $gn52 0></if><else><if ($gn53 > 0)><if $gn4><sheet GCRankGridaniaFemaleText $gn53 0><else><sheet GCRankGridaniaMaleText $gn53 0></if><else><if ($gn54 > 0)><if $gn4><sheet GCRankUldahFemaleText $gn54 0><else><sheet GCRankUldahMaleText $gn54 0></if></if></if></if> <split " " 2><string $gs1></split>. Die Staatstaler sind dein.
#. fr: Fé<shy>li<shy>ci<shy>ta<shy>tions, <if ($gn52 > 0)><if $gn4><sheet GCRankLimsaFemaleText $gn52 0><else><sheet GCRankLimsaMaleText $gn52 0></if><else><if ($gn53 > 0)><if $gn4><sheet GCRankGridaniaFemaleText $gn53 0><else><sheet GCRankGridaniaMaleText $gn53 0></if><else><if ($gn54 > 0)><if $gn4><sheet GCRankUldahFemaleText $gn54 0><else><sheet GCRankUldahMaleText $gn54 0></if></if></if></if>, tu as fait du bon travail<nbsp>! Prends tes sceaux de compagnie.
#. column 30: Here for a company leve? You know the drill.
#. column 31: I've no time for those who've never bothered to take up a levequest.
#. column 32: I expect you back in one piece, <if ($gn52 > 0)><sheet GCRankLimsaMaleText $gn52 0></if><if ($gn53 > 0)><sheet GCRankGridaniaMaleText $gn53 0></if><if ($gn54 > 0)><sheet GCRankUldahMaleText $gn54 0></if>.
#. column 33: I've no time for those who've yet to butt horns with a hapalit.
#. column 35: I can respect a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> who chooses to pledge <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> allegiance to none. But I cannot issue Grand Company leves to that <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if>.
#. column 36: I have no words for those not yet the rank of chief sergeant...except for <i>those</i> words.
#. column 37: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:32:0:34"
msgid "You look no worse for the wear. Not enough challenge, was it?"
msgstr "Выглядите вполне целым. Слишком лёгкое задание, что ли?"

#. ja: 小官は「グランドカンパニーリーヴ」の発行担当！<br>この任務を請け負うことができるのは、<br>いずれかのグランドカンパニー所属者のみであります！
#. de: Hier werden Staatserlasse vergeben! Werde Mitglied in einer der Staatlichen Ge<shy>sell<shy>schaften, oder du gehst leer aus.
#. fr: Tu veux que je te propose des mandats de grande compagnie<nbsp>? Désolé, mais je peux pas confier des missions aux aventuriers qui ont pas encore prêté allégeance à une des trois or<shy>ga<shy>ni<shy>sa<shy>tions de l'Alliance éorzéenne.
#. column 30: Here for a company leve? You know the drill.
#. column 31: I've no time for those who've never bothered to take up a levequest.
#. column 32: I expect you back in one piece, <if ($gn52 > 0)><sheet GCRankLimsaMaleText $gn52 0></if><if ($gn53 > 0)><sheet GCRankGridaniaMaleText $gn53 0></if><if ($gn54 > 0)><sheet GCRankUldahMaleText $gn54 0></if>.
#. column 33: I've no time for those who've yet to butt horns with a hapalit.
#. column 34: You look no worse for the wear. Not enough challenge, was it?
#. column 36: I have no words for those not yet the rank of chief sergeant...except for <i>those</i> words.
#. column 37: 0
#. macro: <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:32:0:35"
msgid "I can respect a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> who chooses to pledge <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> allegiance to none. But I cannot issue Grand Company leves to that <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if>."
msgstr "Я уважаю <if $gn4>девушку<else>парня</if>, решившую <if $gn4>не присягать никому<else>не присягать никому</if>. Но такому <if $gn4>человеку<else>человеку</if> поручений Великой компании не выдаю."

#. ja: モードゥナ地方における任務は、<br>いずれも厳しいものばかりなのであります！<br>「准士」以上の方にのみ、発行しているのであります！
#. de: Die Missionen hier sind hart. Wer nicht mindestens den Rang eines Erleuchteten Schlangenjüngers oder eines Großsturmmaats oder eines Phönixgefreiten hat, braucht gar nicht erst anzutreten.
#. fr: Tu veux que je te propose des mandats de grande compagnie<nbsp>? Désolé, mais je peux pas confier des missions aux recrues qui ont pas au moins le grade de major. Demande une promotion et reviens me voir<nbsp>!
#. column 30: Here for a company leve? You know the drill.
#. column 31: I've no time for those who've never bothered to take up a levequest.
#. column 32: I expect you back in one piece, <if ($gn52 > 0)><sheet GCRankLimsaMaleText $gn52 0></if><if ($gn53 > 0)><sheet GCRankGridaniaMaleText $gn53 0></if><if ($gn54 > 0)><sheet GCRankUldahMaleText $gn54 0></if>.
#. column 33: I've no time for those who've yet to butt horns with a hapalit.
#. column 34: You look no worse for the wear. Not enough challenge, was it?
#. column 35: I can respect a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> who chooses to pledge <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> allegiance to none. But I cannot issue Grand Company leves to that <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if>.
#. column 37: 0
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:32:0:36"
msgid "I have no words for those not yet the rank of chief sergeant...except for <i>those</i> words."
msgstr "Не дослужились до старшего сержанта? Тогда мне нечего вам сказать... кроме <i>этих</i> слов."

#. ja: こちらでは総長の発案による、<br>「神殿騎士団リーヴ」の発行業務を行っております。
#. de: Guten <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>Abend<else>Morgen</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>Tag<else>Abend</if></if>! Ich stehe im Dienst der Kongregation der Tempelritter und vergebe im Auftrag des Großmeisters die Ishgarder Freibriefe.
#. fr: <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>Bonsoir<else>Bonjour</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>Bonjour<else>Bonsoir</if></if> aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>, je suis le chevalier Eloin des templiers. Par ordre du capitaine général, j'ai été chargé de gérer les mandats ishgardais.
#. column 31: You seem barely able to walk, let alone wield a sword or sorcery. Begone.
#. column 32: May the Fury give you strength.
#. column 33: The Temple Knights will not waste time entertaining untested whelps, no matter how willing they may be.
#. column 34: Word of your performance in the field has been received. I shall prepare your reward accordingly.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: The levemetes report that not only did you encounter a wanted mark, but slew the bastard, as well. I applaud your bravery, adventurer.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:33:0:30"
msgid "The lord commander seeks those willing and able to pledge their blades in service to Halone. They need not be of Ishgard, only of sound body and mind."
msgstr "Командующий ищет тех, кто готов служить Халоне и владеет мечом. Неважно, ишгардцы вы или нет, главное — быть крепкими телом и духом."

#. ja: 腕が立ち、信頼の置ける者がいれば、<br>この任務を任せることができるのですが……。
#. de: Ihr seht leider nicht so aus, als könnte man Euch bereits einen Freibrief anvertrauen. Ihr solltet erst noch ein wenig Erfahrung sammeln.
#. fr: Il s'agit de missions destinés aux gens qui ont démontré leurs capacités et leur valeur, mais je crains que vous ne soyez pas encore prêt<if $gn4>e</if> pour cela...
#. column 30: The lord commander seeks those willing and able to pledge their blades in service to Halone. They need not be of Ishgard, only of sound body and mind.
#. column 32: May the Fury give you strength.
#. column 33: The Temple Knights will not waste time entertaining untested whelps, no matter how willing they may be.
#. column 34: Word of your performance in the field has been received. I shall prepare your reward accordingly.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: The levemetes report that not only did you encounter a wanted mark, but slew the bastard, as well. I applaud your bravery, adventurer.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:33:0:31"
msgid "You seem barely able to walk, let alone wield a sword or sorcery. Begone."
msgstr "Ты едва на ногах стоишь, куда уж тебе мечом махать или колдовать. Проваливай."

#. ja: 無事の帰還をお待ちしています。<br>戦神「ハルオーネ」の加護あらんことを！
#. de: Ich erwarte Eure Rückkehr. Möge Halone Euch beistehen.
#. fr: Je vous souhaite bon courage, et que Hamone veille sur vous<nbsp>!
#. column 30: The lord commander seeks those willing and able to pledge their blades in service to Halone. They need not be of Ishgard, only of sound body and mind.
#. column 31: You seem barely able to walk, let alone wield a sword or sorcery. Begone.
#. column 33: The Temple Knights will not waste time entertaining untested whelps, no matter how willing they may be.
#. column 34: Word of your performance in the field has been received. I shall prepare your reward accordingly.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: The levemetes report that not only did you encounter a wanted mark, but slew the bastard, as well. I applaud your bravery, adventurer.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:33:0:32"
msgid "May the Fury give you strength."
msgstr "Пусть Воительница придаст тебе сил."

#. ja: 腕が立ち、信頼の置ける者がいれば、<br>この任務を任せることができるのですが……。
#. de: Ihr seht leider nicht so aus, als könnte man Euch bereits einen Freibrief anvertrauen. Ihr solltet erst noch ein wenig Erfahrung sammeln.
#. fr: J'aimerais pouvoir vous confier une de nos missions, mais je crains que vous n'ayez pas encore fait vos preuves...
#. column 30: The lord commander seeks those willing and able to pledge their blades in service to Halone. They need not be of Ishgard, only of sound body and mind.
#. column 31: You seem barely able to walk, let alone wield a sword or sorcery. Begone.
#. column 32: May the Fury give you strength.
#. column 34: Word of your performance in the field has been received. I shall prepare your reward accordingly.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: The levemetes report that not only did you encounter a wanted mark, but slew the bastard, as well. I applaud your bravery, adventurer.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:33:0:33"
msgid "The Temple Knights will not waste time entertaining untested whelps, no matter how willing they may be."
msgstr "Храмовые рыцари не станут тратить время на сопливых новичков, как бы те ни рвались в бой."

#. ja: 任務の達成を確認しました！<br>皇都への貢献を認め、報酬を支給しましょう！
#. de: Ich gratuliere Euch zum erfolgreichen Abschluss des Auftrages! Bitte lasst mich Euch die versprochene Belohnung aushändigen.
#. fr: Je confirme, vous avez réussi la mission qui vous avait été confiée. Tenez, voici votre récompense<nbsp>!
#. column 30: The lord commander seeks those willing and able to pledge their blades in service to Halone. They need not be of Ishgard, only of sound body and mind.
#. column 31: You seem barely able to walk, let alone wield a sword or sorcery. Begone.
#. column 32: May the Fury give you strength.
#. column 33: The Temple Knights will not waste time entertaining untested whelps, no matter how willing they may be.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: The levemetes report that not only did you encounter a wanted mark, but slew the bastard, as well. I applaud your bravery, adventurer.
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:33:0:34"
msgid "Word of your performance in the field has been received. I shall prepare your reward accordingly."
msgstr "До меня дошли вести о твоих успехах. Приготовлю тебе награду."

#. ja: なんと、手配中の賞金首を仕留めたと？<br>でしたら、報酬を上乗せしなければいけませんね。
#. de: Natürlich erhaltet Ihr auch das Kopfgeld für das gesuchte Ziel, das Ihr ausgeschalten habt.
#. fr: Je constate que vous avez également abattu un ennemi dont nous autres templiers avions mis la tête à prix. Dans ce cas, je vais augmenter votre récompense comme il se doit<nbsp>!
#. column 30: The lord commander seeks those willing and able to pledge their blades in service to Halone. They need not be of Ishgard, only of sound body and mind.
#. column 31: You seem barely able to walk, let alone wield a sword or sorcery. Begone.
#. column 32: May the Fury give you strength.
#. column 33: The Temple Knights will not waste time entertaining untested whelps, no matter how willing they may be.
#. column 34: Word of your performance in the field has been received. I shall prepare your reward accordingly.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:33:0:37"
msgid "The levemetes report that not only did you encounter a wanted mark, but slew the bastard, as well. I applaud your bravery, adventurer."
msgstr "Говорят, ты не только наткнулся на разыскиваемого преступника, но и прикончил его. Вот это храбрость, искатель приключений!"

#. ja: 冒険者ギルドの活動範囲を広げるために、<br>本部からの指示で、ここクガネに窓口を開設したんだ。<br>よかったら、力を貸してくれよな！
#. de: Die Aben<shy>teurer<shy>gilde von Eorzea hat mich nach Kugane entsandt, um ihren Bekanntheitsgrad zu steigern und - natürlich ganz uneigennützig - unseren Freunden im Fernen Osten bei ihren täglichen Arbeiten und Sorgen zu helfen.
#. fr: La guilde des aventuriers cherche à élargir sa zone d'activité. C'est pour ça qu'elle a décidé d'ouvrir un comptoir pour les mandats ici même à Kugane<nbsp>!
#. column 31: I appreciate your enthusiasm, but without the proper credentials, I cannot risk assigning you a task that─if mishandled─could reflect poorly on the Adventurers' Guild.
#. column 32: How fares the task? The people here can be distrusting of foreigners at times, even if our intentions are well and good, but the guild is positive they will warm to us if we show them we can be trusted.
#. column 33: I appreciate your enthusiasm, but without the proper credentials, I cannot risk assigning you a task that─if mishandled─could reflect poorly on the Adventurers' Guild.
#. column 34: With each of these tasks completed, we earn a little more of our Eastern neighbors' trust. You have done a noble thing here today, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. I hope to see you again soon.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:34:0:30"
msgid "I have been dispatched here to Kugane by the Eorzean Adventurers' Guild to spread recognition of our establishment while helping us gain a foothold here in the Far East. And what better way to the locals' hearts than by offering them our aid─through guildleves, of course!"
msgstr "Гильдия искателей приключений Эорзеи отправила меня в Куганэ, чтобы рассказать о себе и помочь нам закрепиться на Дальнем Востоке. А что лучше расположит к нам местных, чем помощь? Конечно же, задания по гильдейским грамотам!"

#. ja: 職人技を持つ冒険者が見つかるといいんだが……。
#. de: Ich freue mich, dass du helfen möchtest. Aber bitte habe Verständnis dafür, dass du deine Eignung erst unter Beweis stellen musst. Die Aben<shy>teurer<shy>gilde kann sich keinen Gesichtsverlust in Hingashi erlauben.
#. fr: Nous recherchons ac<shy>tu<shy>el<shy>le<shy>ment des artisans compétents pour nous aider.
#. column 30: I have been dispatched here to Kugane by the Eorzean Adventurers' Guild to spread recognition of our establishment while helping us gain a foothold here in the Far East. And what better way to the locals' hearts than by offering them our aid─through guildleves, of course!
#. column 32: How fares the task? The people here can be distrusting of foreigners at times, even if our intentions are well and good, but the guild is positive they will warm to us if we show them we can be trusted.
#. column 33: I appreciate your enthusiasm, but without the proper credentials, I cannot risk assigning you a task that─if mishandled─could reflect poorly on the Adventurers' Guild.
#. column 34: With each of these tasks completed, we earn a little more of our Eastern neighbors' trust. You have done a noble thing here today, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. I hope to see you again soon.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:34:0:31"
msgid "I appreciate your enthusiasm, but without the proper credentials, I cannot risk assigning you a task that─if mishandled─could reflect poorly on the Adventurers' Guild."
msgstr "Ценю твой пыл, но без нужных рекомендаций не могу поручить тебе задание. Если ты с ним не справишься, это бросит тень на гильдию искателей приключений."

#. ja: 依頼の方は順調かい？<br>そうだと信じているんだが……大丈夫だよな？
#. de: Wie kommst du zurecht? Manche Hinganer fühlen sich nicht wohl dabei, einem Fremden wichtige Arbeiten zu überlassen. Aber wenn du ein freundliches Gesicht machst und dir Mühe gibst, werden sie mehr und mehr Vertrauen in die Abenteurer unserer Gilde fassen.
#. fr: Ça se passe bien avec les mandats<nbsp>? J'imagine que ça ne doit pas être toujours très facile, mais je suis sûr que vous vous en sortez à merveille<nbsp>!
#. column 30: I have been dispatched here to Kugane by the Eorzean Adventurers' Guild to spread recognition of our establishment while helping us gain a foothold here in the Far East. And what better way to the locals' hearts than by offering them our aid─through guildleves, of course!
#. column 31: I appreciate your enthusiasm, but without the proper credentials, I cannot risk assigning you a task that─if mishandled─could reflect poorly on the Adventurers' Guild.
#. column 33: I appreciate your enthusiasm, but without the proper credentials, I cannot risk assigning you a task that─if mishandled─could reflect poorly on the Adventurers' Guild.
#. column 34: With each of these tasks completed, we earn a little more of our Eastern neighbors' trust. You have done a noble thing here today, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. I hope to see you again soon.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:34:0:32"
msgid "How fares the task? The people here can be distrusting of foreigners at times, even if our intentions are well and good, but the guild is positive they will warm to us if we show them we can be trusted."
msgstr "Как продвигается задание? Местные порой не доверяют чужакам, даже если те желают им добра. Но в гильдии уверены: если мы покажем, что нам можно доверять, они к нам потеплеют."

#. ja: 職人技を持つ冒険者が見つかるといいんだが……。
#. de: Ich freue mich, dass du helfen möchtest. Aber bitte habe Verständnis dafür, dass du deine Eignung erst unter Beweis stellen musst. Die Aben<shy>teurer<shy>gilde kann sich keinen Gesichtsverlust in Hingashi erlauben.
#. fr: Nous avons vraiment besoin d'artisans compétents pour nous aider.
#. column 30: I have been dispatched here to Kugane by the Eorzean Adventurers' Guild to spread recognition of our establishment while helping us gain a foothold here in the Far East. And what better way to the locals' hearts than by offering them our aid─through guildleves, of course!
#. column 31: I appreciate your enthusiasm, but without the proper credentials, I cannot risk assigning you a task that─if mishandled─could reflect poorly on the Adventurers' Guild.
#. column 32: How fares the task? The people here can be distrusting of foreigners at times, even if our intentions are well and good, but the guild is positive they will warm to us if we show them we can be trusted.
#. column 34: With each of these tasks completed, we earn a little more of our Eastern neighbors' trust. You have done a noble thing here today, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. I hope to see you again soon.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:34:0:33"
msgid "I appreciate your enthusiasm, but without the proper credentials, I cannot risk assigning you a task that─if mishandled─could reflect poorly on the Adventurers' Guild."
msgstr "Ценю твой пыл, но без нужных рекомендаций не могу поручить тебе задание. Если ты с ним не справишься, это бросит тень на гильдию искателей приключений."

#. ja: よし、依頼の達成を確認したぞ。<br>お待ちかねの報酬だ、受け取ってくれ！
#. de: Mit jeder bewältigten Aufgabe verdienen wir uns ein bisschen mehr Vertrauen bei unseren hinganischen Freunden. Du hast dazu einen wichtigen Beitrag geleistet, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. Komm bald wieder.
#. fr: Vous avez fait un travail remarquable... Voilà la récompense<nbsp>!
#. column 30: I have been dispatched here to Kugane by the Eorzean Adventurers' Guild to spread recognition of our establishment while helping us gain a foothold here in the Far East. And what better way to the locals' hearts than by offering them our aid─through guildleves, of course!
#. column 31: I appreciate your enthusiasm, but without the proper credentials, I cannot risk assigning you a task that─if mishandled─could reflect poorly on the Adventurers' Guild.
#. column 32: How fares the task? The people here can be distrusting of foreigners at times, even if our intentions are well and good, but the guild is positive they will warm to us if we show them we can be trusted.
#. column 33: I appreciate your enthusiasm, but without the proper credentials, I cannot risk assigning you a task that─if mishandled─could reflect poorly on the Adventurers' Guild.
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: 0
#. macro: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split> — the first name of the player character (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <string $gs1> — a text value passed to the string; value = global text 1 (the name of the player character) (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:34:0:34"
msgid "With each of these tasks completed, we earn a little more of our Eastern neighbors' trust. You have done a noble thing here today, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>. I hope to see you again soon."
msgstr "С каждым выполненным заданием соседи с Востока доверяют нам всё больше. Ты сегодня сделал доброе дело, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>. Надеюсь, скоро снова увидимся."

#. ja: ミーン工芸館に寄せられる大量の仕事を、<br>登録している職人に、リーヴとして斡旋しているよ。<br>アンタも、ひとつやっていかないかい？
#. de: Crystarium ist ein Ort, an dem jeder seinen Teil tut, und die Manufaktur der Gemeinschaft bietet jedem dazu Gelegenheit. Willst du nicht auch ein paar Dinge erledigen, die der Allgemeinheit zugutekommen?
#. fr: La halle du Juste a besoin d'artisans talentueux prêts à relever toutes sortes de défis<nbsp>! Ça vous dirait de prendre un mandat en charge, <if $gn4>voyageuse<else>voyageur</if><nbsp>?
#. column 31: You dabble in trades? Could've fooled me. Are you sure?
#. column 32: We're all looking forward to seeing what you bring us, friend!
#. column 33: You dabble in trades? Could've fooled me. Are you sure?
#. column 34: Came through, as we knew you would. Here's your reward. Don't be a stranger!
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:35:0:30"
msgid "The Mean's looking for a few good artisans to handle some of the work they can't. We'd be much obliged if you'd fill a leve or two."
msgstr "В Мине ищут хороших мастеров, чтобы те взялись за работу, с которой сами не справляются. Будем очень признательны, если выполнишь пару поручений."

#. ja: リーヴに興味がある職人はいないものか……。
#. de: In der Manufaktur kann jeder helfen. Jeder, der die Grundeignung erfüllt. Bitte sieh doch später noch einmal vorbei.
#. fr: Quelqu'un serait-il intéressé par un mandat<nbsp>? N'hésitez pas à demander, j'en ai plein en stock<nbsp>!
#. column 30: The Mean's looking for a few good artisans to handle some of the work they can't. We'd be much obliged if you'd fill a leve or two.
#. column 32: We're all looking forward to seeing what you bring us, friend!
#. column 33: You dabble in trades? Could've fooled me. Are you sure?
#. column 34: Came through, as we knew you would. Here's your reward. Don't be a stranger!
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:35:0:31"
msgid "You dabble in trades? Could've fooled me. Are you sure?"
msgstr "Ты, значит, ремеслом балуешься? Что-то не скажешь. Уверен, что справишься?"

#. ja: さて、頼んだ仕事の方はどうだい？<br>しっかり頼むよ！
#. de: Wie läuft es mit den Arbeiten? Erledigst du deine Aufgaben, um der Gemeinschaft zu helfen? In Crystarium ist Platz für jeden, aber wir erwarten, dass man seinen Anteil tut.
#. fr: Alors, ce mandat, ça avance<nbsp>? Je compte sur vous<nbsp>!
#. column 30: The Mean's looking for a few good artisans to handle some of the work they can't. We'd be much obliged if you'd fill a leve or two.
#. column 31: You dabble in trades? Could've fooled me. Are you sure?
#. column 33: You dabble in trades? Could've fooled me. Are you sure?
#. column 34: Came through, as we knew you would. Here's your reward. Don't be a stranger!
#. column 35: 0
#. column 36: 0
#. column 37: 0
msgctxt "GuildleveAssignmentTalk:35:0:32"
msgid "We're all looking forward to seeing what you bring us, friend!"
msgstr "Все мы с нетерпением ждём, что ты для нас приготовишь, дружище!"

#. ja: リーヴに興味がある職人はいないものか……。
#. de: In der Manufaktur kann jeder helfen. Jeder, der die Grundeignung erfüllt. Bitte sieh doch später noch einmal vorbei.
